1
00:00:01,168 --> 00:00:04,538
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:04,572 --> 00:00:07,408
♪ SOMEWHERE IN TIME
AND SPACE ♪

3
00:00:07,442 --> 00:00:10,645
♪ MIKE NELSON
AND HIS ROBOT PALS ♪

4
00:00:10,678 --> 00:00:13,682
♪ ARE CAUGHT IN
AN ENDLESS CHASE ♪

5
00:00:13,715 --> 00:00:16,683
♪ PURSUED BY A WOMAN
WHOSE NAME IS PEARL ♪

6
00:00:16,718 --> 00:00:19,920
♪ AN EVIL GAL WHO WANTS
TO RULE THE WORLD ♪

7
00:00:19,953 --> 00:00:22,823
♪ SHE THREW A FEW THINGS
IN HER PURSE ♪

8
00:00:22,857 --> 00:00:24,492
♪ AND IN HER ROCKET SHIP
SHE HUNTS HIM ♪

9
00:00:24,525 --> 00:00:26,493
♪ ALL ACROSS THE UNIVERSE ♪

10
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:29,330
[PEARL]
I'LL GET YOU!

11
00:00:29,363 --> 00:00:32,200
♪ I'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

12
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:35,737
♪ THE WORST I CAN FIND--
LA LA LA ♪

13
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:38,607
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

14
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:41,743
♪ AND I'LL MONITOR HIS MIND--
LA LA LA ♪

15
00:00:41,777 --> 00:00:44,612
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND,
MIKE CAN'T CONTROL ♪

16
00:00:44,645 --> 00:00:48,115
♪ WHERE THE MOVIES BEGIN
OR END-- LA LA LA ♪

17
00:00:48,148 --> 00:00:51,052
♪ HE'LL TRY TO KEEP
HIS SANITY ♪

18
00:00:51,085 --> 00:00:53,555
♪ WITH THE HELP
OF HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

19
00:00:56,157 --> 00:00:57,492
♪ ROBOT ROLL CALL ♪

20
00:00:57,525 --> 00:00:59,193
YOU'RE ON!

21
00:00:59,227 --> 00:01:00,462
OH, MY STARS!

22
00:01:00,495 --> 00:01:02,063
CHECK ME OUT!

23
00:01:02,097 --> 00:01:03,532
I'M DIFFERENT!

24
00:01:03,565 --> 00:01:04,965
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW ♪

25
00:01:04,998 --> 00:01:06,667
♪ HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

26
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:09,837
♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS--
LA LA LA ♪

27
00:01:09,870 --> 00:01:12,640
♪ JUST REPEAT TO YOURSELF,
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

28
00:01:12,673 --> 00:01:15,943
♪ I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX" ♪

29
00:01:15,977 --> 00:01:19,013
♪ FOR MYSTERY
SCIENCE THEATER ♪

30
00:01:19,047 --> 00:01:22,583
♪ 3000 ♪

31
00:01:35,095 --> 00:01:38,365
YOU GUYS DID A LITTLE FILM
CALLED OPERATION DUMBO DROP.

32
00:01:38,398 --> 00:01:41,202
- TALK ABOUT THAT.
- SNAP OUT OF IT, MIKE.

33
00:01:41,235 --> 00:01:42,703
HI, EVERYBODY. WELCOME.

34
00:01:42,737 --> 00:01:45,340
MIKE TRIPPED OVER
MY YAM COLLECTION,
FELL ON HIS HEAD,

35
00:01:45,373 --> 00:01:47,508
NOW THE POOR DOPE
THINKS HE JAMES LIPTON,

36
00:01:47,542 --> 00:01:49,777
HOST OF THAT
INSIDE THE ACTOR'S STUDIO
PROGRAM

37
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:51,745
ON, UH, OH, I DON'T KNOW,
SOME CHANNEL.

38
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:53,682
HELL, I DON'T WATCH CABLE.

39
00:01:53,715 --> 00:01:56,417
THEN, OF COURSE, YOU HAD
A SMALL, BUT CRUCIAL, ROLE

40
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:58,452
IN HAROLD ROBBINS'
THE LONELY LADY.

41
00:01:58,487 --> 00:02:00,455
THE STAR, OF COURSE,
PIA ZADORA.

42
00:02:00,488 --> 00:02:02,223
YOU TWO BECAME SOUL MATES.

43
00:02:02,257 --> 00:02:04,458
NO WE DIDN'T!
STOP IT, MIKE!

44
00:02:04,492 --> 00:02:06,360
SEE, NOW HE THINKS CROW
IS RAY LIOTTA.

45
00:02:06,393 --> 00:02:08,095
AND HE'S TRYING
TO INTERVIEW HIM,

46
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:11,332
AND IT'S DRIVING CROW CRAZY.
AND, WELL, LET'S WATCH,
SHALL WE?

47
00:02:11,365 --> 00:02:13,835
UNLAWFUL ENTRY, OF COURSE,
A BRILLIANT TURN.

48
00:02:13,902 --> 00:02:15,670
A BREAKOUT ROLE FOR YOU.

49
00:02:15,703 --> 00:02:18,973
YOU USED TO TRADE SOUP RECIPES
WITH KURT RUSSELL ON THE SET.

50
00:02:19,007 --> 00:02:21,675
- TALK ABOUT THAT.
- NO! MIKE, YOU'RE NOT WELL.

51
00:02:21,708 --> 00:02:25,180
WHOOPI GOLDBERG TOLD ME
YOU SMELL LIKE APPLES. TRUE?

52
00:02:25,213 --> 00:02:27,515
WHAT? THAT DOES IT, MIKE.
I'M GETTING THE CLOWN HAMMER.

53
00:02:27,548 --> 00:02:30,150
ARE YOU REALLY A GOOD FELLA?
UH-HUH.

54
00:02:30,185 --> 00:02:34,322
GIVE US THE INSIDE STORY
ON TOM HULCE'S DOG. UH-HUH.

55
00:02:34,355 --> 00:02:37,225
JOE PESCI'S MOTHER
MADE YOU WEEP, HOW?

56
00:02:37,258 --> 00:02:39,327
- SORRY, WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.
- YOU CALLED KEVIN DOBSON

57
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:42,263
YOUR REAL REASON FOR LIVING.
CAN YOU TELL ME WHY?

58
00:02:42,297 --> 00:02:44,832
- SAD, REALLY.
- MM-HM. YES.

59
00:02:44,865 --> 00:02:47,668
♪♪

60
00:02:52,173 --> 00:02:55,543
STUDENTS, PLEASE JOIN ME
IN THANKING MR. WILLIAM KATT.

61
00:02:55,577 --> 00:02:58,713
TRULY, YOU ARE
THE GREATEST AMERICAN HERO.

62
00:02:58,747 --> 00:03:00,382
[METAL CLANK]

63
00:03:00,415 --> 00:03:01,950
THERE HE GOES.
[LAUGHTER]

64
00:03:01,983 --> 00:03:05,553
BOY, I SURE HATED TO DO THAT.

65
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:09,690
GUYS! WHAT ARE YOU DRESSING ME
AS JAMES LIPTON FOR,
YA WEIRDOES?

66
00:03:09,723 --> 00:03:11,625
WE HAVE TO GET GOING
ON OUR ESCAPE PLAN.

67
00:03:11,658 --> 00:03:13,327
WELL, I'M SORRY-- HEY!

68
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:16,263
CROW, HAVE THE NANITES
CONSTRUCTED MY MODULAR DESCENT
UNIT YET?

69
00:03:16,297 --> 00:03:18,633
UH, YEAH, SURE. WHY NOT?

70
00:03:18,667 --> 00:03:21,568
THEN, SINCE WE ARE IN HIGH
GEOSYNCHRONOUS ORBIT,

71
00:03:21,602 --> 00:03:24,738
I WILL DESCEND AND JUMP OFF
ON SOME UNKNOWN LOCATION

72
00:03:24,772 --> 00:03:26,340
ON PRESENT DAY PLANET EARTH.

73
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:28,175
THEN, OF COURSE, YOU'LL ALERT
THE AUTHORITIES

74
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:32,380
- AND RESCUE US, RIGHT?
- UH, TIME PERMITTING, SURE.

75
00:03:32,413 --> 00:03:33,848
- THAT SOUNDS REASONABLE. HEY!
- HEY!

76
00:03:33,882 --> 00:03:36,650
BOY, IT'S REALLY
A LONG WAY DOWN.

77
00:03:36,683 --> 00:03:39,420
HAVE NOT MADE CONTACT
WITH EARTH YET. OVER.

78
00:03:39,453 --> 00:03:42,823
KEEP GOING,
YOU BIG DOPE. OVER.

79
00:03:42,857 --> 00:03:45,627
- WHAT WAS THAT? OVER.
- NOTHING. OVER.

80
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,428
I THOUGHT
YOU SAID SOMETHING. OVER.

81
00:03:47,462 --> 00:03:50,298
- NO. OVER.
- BUT I SAID IT WAS A LONG WAY
DOWN AND THEN--

82
00:03:50,332 --> 00:03:52,933
LOOK, WOULD YOU
JUST DROP IT! OVER.

83
00:03:52,967 --> 00:03:56,570
JEEZ, OKAY. ALL RIGHT.
THROUGH THE ATMOSPHERE NOW,

84
00:03:56,603 --> 00:03:59,907
AND AM APPROACHING
A LARGE STRUCTURE OF SOME SORT.

85
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:02,410
I AM OPENING A HATCH
OF SOME SORT,

86
00:04:02,443 --> 00:04:05,480
AND AM DROPPING
THE LADDER IN.

87
00:04:05,513 --> 00:04:08,348
I WILL ENTER
THE ACTUAL STRUCTURE NOW.

88
00:04:08,382 --> 00:04:10,352
WHICH APPEARS TO BE
A BARN OF SOME SORT,

89
00:04:10,385 --> 00:04:13,020
OR A-- NO, IT'S AN EATERY.
IT IS AN EATERY.

90
00:04:13,053 --> 00:04:15,055
I WILL APPROACH
ONE OF THE PATRONS,

91
00:04:15,088 --> 00:04:18,358
AND ATTEMPT TO GATHER
INFORMATION ON MY WHERE--

92
00:04:18,392 --> 00:04:19,860
WHEREABOUTS.

93
00:04:19,893 --> 00:04:22,563
- BRAIN GUY.
- YUP.

94
00:04:22,597 --> 00:04:24,898
[MIKE STAMMERS]

95
00:04:24,932 --> 00:04:27,002
AAH! I'LL JUST GET BACK UP
AND WATCH MY MOVIE.

96
00:04:27,035 --> 00:04:29,237
- WHICH IS WHAT AGAIN?
- WEREWOLF.

97
00:04:29,270 --> 00:04:31,105
WEREWOLF, RIGHT.

98
00:04:31,138 --> 00:04:33,440
BRAIN GUY, YOU WOULDN'T WANT
TO BEAM ME BACK UP THERE,
WOULD YOU?

99
00:04:33,473 --> 00:04:35,042
- NO.
- OKAY, DIDN'T THINK SO.

100
00:04:35,075 --> 00:04:38,212
JUST CHECKING. I'LL GET BACK UP,
AND WATCH MY...

101
00:04:38,245 --> 00:04:40,815
[MIKE WHIMPERS]

102
00:04:40,848 --> 00:04:43,918
[GROWLS]

103
00:04:43,952 --> 00:04:46,887
UH, I'M GONNA SCRUB
THIS ONE, GUYS. OVER.

104
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:49,957
UH, YUP. GET PASTY-BUTT
UP HERE NOW. OVER.

105
00:04:49,990 --> 00:04:51,325
UH, WHAT'S THAT? OVER.

106
00:04:51,358 --> 00:04:53,762
- [ALARM BUZZES]
- UH, NEVER MIND. MOVIE SIGN!

107
00:04:53,795 --> 00:04:56,230
- OVER AND OUT.
- I SWEAR, IS THIS SOMETHING
ABOUT--

108
00:04:56,263 --> 00:04:58,132
HEY, GET BACK HERE.

109
00:05:08,677 --> 00:05:10,143
JEEZ. POOR GUY.

110
00:05:10,177 --> 00:05:11,278
[WOLF HOWLS]

111
00:05:11,312 --> 00:05:13,080
I DON'T KNOW.
YOU HAD HIM LAST!

112
00:05:13,113 --> 00:05:15,282
YOU CAN'T SAY THAT.
YOU'RE GONNA GET IN TROUBLE.

113
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:17,285
THAT'S A REALLY STUPID JOKE,
AND I'M GONNA TELL MIKE.

114
00:05:17,318 --> 00:05:19,720
I DON'T CARE.
WHAT'S MIKE GONNA DO ANYWAY?

115
00:05:19,753 --> 00:05:21,255
- HEY, GUYS.
- AAH!

116
00:05:21,288 --> 00:05:23,090
MIKE, THE TITLE CAME UP,
AND IT SAID WEREWOLF.

117
00:05:23,123 --> 00:05:25,092
AND THE SERVO SAID,
"I DON'T KNOW,
YOU HAD HIM LAST."

118
00:05:25,125 --> 00:05:27,295
AND I-- I THINK THAT WAS
A REALLY STUPID JOKE.

119
00:05:27,328 --> 00:05:29,130
THAT'S PRETTY FUNNY.
I LIKE THAT.

120
00:05:29,163 --> 00:05:30,330
- THANK YOU.
- YEAH, THAT'S WHAT I MEANT.

121
00:05:30,365 --> 00:05:32,367
I LIKED IT.

122
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:33,835
- GOOD ONE, SERVO.
- THANK YOU.

123
00:05:33,868 --> 00:05:35,068
♪♪ [NATIVE AMERICAN MUSIC]

124
00:05:35,102 --> 00:05:39,240
MUST BE A SONG ABOUT
HOW LOOSE THEIR SLOTS ARE.

125
00:05:39,273 --> 00:05:44,412
AH, ONE OF
THE LESSER ESTEVEZES.

126
00:05:44,445 --> 00:05:47,248
AND NOW THE LADIES!

127
00:05:47,282 --> 00:05:51,252
SO FAR, THE STAR POWER CONSISTS
OF CHARLIE SHEEN'S UNCLE.

128
00:05:57,525 --> 00:06:00,360
UM, ARE THEY JUMPING ROPE?

129
00:06:00,395 --> 00:06:03,263
NOT LAST NIGHT,
BUT THE NIGHT BEFORE,

130
00:06:03,297 --> 00:06:06,667
24 ROBBERS COME KNOCKING
AT MY DOOR.

131
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,635
JUMPING ROPE.

132
00:06:08,668 --> 00:06:12,773
AH, THE POOR THING HAS TMJ.
LOOK AT THAT.

133
00:06:12,807 --> 00:06:15,710
KEITH BILDERBECK.
BUILDING A BETTER BECK FOR YOU.

134
00:06:15,743 --> 00:06:19,847
NELSONE! GOOD ONE THERE!

135
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:24,985
I KNEW IT HAD TONY ZARINDAST'S
STINK ALL OVER IT.

136
00:06:25,018 --> 00:06:28,790
BROUGHT TO YOU BY THE...

137
00:06:28,823 --> 00:06:30,792
FEATURING
THE BULGARIAN WOMEN'S CHOIR

138
00:06:30,825 --> 00:06:34,695
RENDITION OF "JINGLE BELLS."

139
00:06:34,728 --> 00:06:36,630
[HUMMING]

140
00:06:36,663 --> 00:06:39,133
MAN, THERE'S JUST TOO MUCH
ZARINDAST IN THIS MOVIE ALREADY.

141
00:06:39,167 --> 00:06:44,705
- MM-HM.
- WHOO.

142
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:48,675
MM, THE SUGAR MINES!

143
00:06:48,708 --> 00:06:51,178
THEY'RE EXCAVATING
A TIRAMISU.

144
00:06:51,212 --> 00:06:54,882
WE FOUND ANOTHER STRATUM
OF LADY FINGERS.

145
00:06:58,218 --> 00:07:01,655
WE GOT THE WORST
TREE FARM EVER.

146
00:07:01,688 --> 00:07:04,058
GIVE ME THAT CANTEEN THERE
WILL YA?

147
00:07:04,092 --> 00:07:06,593
HEY, GERONIMO!
GET BACK TO WORK.

148
00:07:06,627 --> 00:07:09,497
YEAH, OKAY, LIEF ERIKSSON.

149
00:07:09,530 --> 00:07:11,332
[GERONIMO LAUGHS]

150
00:07:11,365 --> 00:07:15,002
CAN'T YOU HEAR ME?
I SAID GET BACK TO WORK.

151
00:07:15,035 --> 00:07:16,803
HEY, MAN...

152
00:07:16,837 --> 00:07:18,705
IT'S HOTTER THAN HELL
OUT HERE.

153
00:07:18,738 --> 00:07:21,375
- TOMMY, COME ON, MAN.
- COME OVER HERE
AND GIVE US A HAND.

154
00:07:21,408 --> 00:07:24,845
JERK! NEEDS TO GET HIS HEAD
STRAIGHTENED OUT OR SOMETHING.

155
00:07:24,878 --> 00:07:26,813
THE HOSER.

156
00:07:26,847 --> 00:07:28,082
TOMMY, COME ON, MAN.

157
00:07:28,115 --> 00:07:29,350
YOU PISS HIM OFF MORE,
HE'S GONNA FIRE US ALL.

158
00:07:29,383 --> 00:07:32,153
COME ON, COME ON.

159
00:07:32,187 --> 00:07:33,988
HEY, WHAT IS THIS?
I GOT SOMETHING.

160
00:07:34,022 --> 00:07:36,557
BE CAREFUL, MAN.
WE DON'T WANT TO DAMAGE IT.

161
00:07:36,557 --> 00:07:39,260
HEY, GET AWAY!
YOU'RE GONNA MESS UP THE FIND.

162
00:07:39,293 --> 00:07:41,862
HEY, I CAN'T SEE HOME PLATE.

163
00:07:41,895 --> 00:07:43,163
HEY, I GOT SOMETHING HERE.

164
00:07:43,197 --> 00:07:48,102
IT'S RON!

165
00:07:48,135 --> 00:07:51,172
HEY, MAN,
CAN'T YOU SEE I'M HURT?

166
00:07:51,205 --> 00:07:53,473
THIS IS WHERE BILLY JACK
SHOULD COME RIDING UP.

167
00:07:53,507 --> 00:07:55,408
DAMN IT!

168
00:07:55,442 --> 00:07:58,980
YOU KNOW,
NEVER PUT MARSHALL TUCKER
IN CHARGE OF YOUR DIG.

169
00:07:59,013 --> 00:08:03,317
SOUNDS LIKE SOMEBODY'S PUNCHING
A SIDE OF BEEF OFF-SCREEN.

170
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:07,388
YURI, STOP IT. STOP IT!

171
00:08:07,422 --> 00:08:09,990
ROCK 'EM SOCK 'EM
ARCHEOLOGISTS.

172
00:08:10,023 --> 00:08:14,062
BROOKS AND DUNN
FINALLY HAVE IT OUT.

173
00:08:14,095 --> 00:08:18,967
AH, FILIPINO CROTCH-FIGHTING.

174
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:22,537
THIS IS A PRODUCTION
OF ROAD HOUSE IN THE PARK.

175
00:08:22,570 --> 00:08:26,073
RAT PATROL SHOULD'VE HUNG IT UP
AFTER THE WAR.

176
00:08:28,977 --> 00:08:33,580
OKAY, JUST STAND THERE
WHILE I PUNCH YOU. THERE.

177
00:08:33,613 --> 00:08:37,318
HEY, HOW ARE THE WAVES TODAY,
YOU GUYS?

178
00:08:37,352 --> 00:08:39,887
THE MAN WITH THE YELLOW HAT
ARRIVES TO CALM THINGS DOWN.

179
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:42,257
OH, GOOD.

180
00:08:45,827 --> 00:08:47,160
DURING THE COURSE
OF THE FIGHT,

181
00:08:47,193 --> 00:08:50,230
THEY STOMPED ALL OVER
THE ARK OF THE COVENANT.

182
00:08:52,333 --> 00:08:56,037
LOUIS LEAKEY IN
EVERY WHICH WAY BUT LOOSE.

183
00:08:58,505 --> 00:09:00,708
UM... ARE WE DONE FIGHTING?

184
00:09:00,742 --> 00:09:04,912
SOMEBODY GOT A, UH,
EMERGENCY KIT AROUND HERE?

185
00:09:04,945 --> 00:09:07,415
VANESSA REDGRAVE
FOR BANANA REPUBLIC.

186
00:09:07,448 --> 00:09:09,583
WHAT'S GOING ON?
WHAT HAPPENED?

187
00:09:13,387 --> 00:09:15,022
FOOL ALMOST DAMAGED
THE FIND.

188
00:09:15,055 --> 00:09:16,090
STAY CALM, YURI.

189
00:09:16,123 --> 00:09:18,892
THIS IS THE MIR
OF ARCHAEOLOGICAL DIGS.

190
00:09:21,362 --> 00:09:24,832
THERE'S QUITE A BIT OF BLOOD.
YOU'LL NEED STITCHES.

191
00:09:24,865 --> 00:09:26,067
YEAH, I THINK YOU'RE RIGHT.

192
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:29,303
WELL, QUITE A BIT
OF RED TEMPERA PAINT ANYWAY.

193
00:09:31,372 --> 00:09:35,208
THERE'S JUST SO MUCH LITTER
ON THE HIGHWAY!

194
00:09:37,345 --> 00:09:38,845
YEAH, I'M JUST
GONNA COVER THIS UP.

195
00:09:38,878 --> 00:09:42,783
FINDS ARE TOO HARD,
TOO MUCH PAPERWORK AND STUFF.

196
00:09:42,817 --> 00:09:44,918
I'M MARTIN SHEEN'S BROTHER,
DOES THAT HELP?

197
00:09:44,952 --> 00:09:47,488
PROFESSOR NOEL, YOU'VE GOT TO
TAKE A LOOK AT THIS.

198
00:09:47,522 --> 00:09:50,190
NOT NOW, YURI,
I'VE GOT A MAN HURT OVER HERE.

199
00:09:50,223 --> 00:09:51,292
ME TOO.

200
00:09:51,325 --> 00:09:53,060
LOOK, BILLY,
TAKE TOMMY INTO TOWN.

201
00:09:53,093 --> 00:09:55,095
GET A DOCTOR,
GET THAT ARM STITCHED UP.

202
00:09:55,128 --> 00:09:57,998
- WE'LL PAY THE BILL.
- SURE.

203
00:09:58,032 --> 00:09:59,733
LAURA DERN PROTOTYPE.

204
00:09:59,767 --> 00:10:02,068
PROFESSOR NOEL,
COME AND TAKE A LOOK AT THIS!

205
00:10:02,102 --> 00:10:07,107
WHAT THE HELL IS IT, YURI,
THAT CAN'T WAIT?

206
00:10:07,140 --> 00:10:11,345
♪ O-CEDAR MAKES
YOUR LIFE EASIER ♪

207
00:10:11,378 --> 00:10:14,982
NO SHOES. HE WAS KILLED
FOR HIS NIKES.

208
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:22,557
WHAT THE HELL?

209
00:10:22,590 --> 00:10:24,892
CALL AN AMBULANCE,
AND MAKE SURE
YOU DON'T MOVE HIS NECK.

210
00:10:24,925 --> 00:10:27,728
- [MUSIC STING]
- CRUISE SHIP TAKING OFF.

211
00:10:27,762 --> 00:10:30,898
- [MUSICAL STING[
- THERE'S ANOTHER ONE.

212
00:10:34,168 --> 00:10:38,605
IT'S STEVEN TYLER'S SKULL!

213
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:40,908
NAALDLOOSHII.

214
00:10:40,942 --> 00:10:44,012
YEAH, BOY,
NAALDLOOSHII FOR ME TOO.

215
00:10:47,382 --> 00:10:50,183
LOOK, UH, JOE, WHY DON'T YOU
CATCH UP WITH THE OTHER GUYS,

216
00:10:50,217 --> 00:10:52,587
AND HELP THEM OUT WITH TOMMY,
ALL RIGHT?

217
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:53,687
IN FACT, BY THE TIME
YOU'RE DONE,

218
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:55,188
MOST OF THIS DAY
WILL BE SHOT,

219
00:10:55,222 --> 00:10:57,123
SO WHY DON'T YOU JUST TAKE
THE REST OF THE AFTERNOON OFF?

220
00:10:57,157 --> 00:11:01,028
IN FACT, WHY DON'T YOU JUST
SIT OUT THE REST OF THE MOVIE?

221
00:11:01,062 --> 00:11:02,295
WELL, GO ON.
YOU BETTER HURRY UP

222
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:06,067
IF YOU'RE GOING TO
CATCH UP WITH THEM.

223
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:10,170
[DOG YELPING]

224
00:11:10,203 --> 00:11:14,875
GO HOME, JOE!
ALL THE WAY. GOOD BOY.

225
00:11:14,908 --> 00:11:17,277
CAN I HAVE IT?
MY DOG NEEDS A NEW HEAD.

226
00:11:17,310 --> 00:11:20,113
- NOEL, WHAT WAS THAT ALL ABOUT?
- I'LL EXPLAIN LATER.

227
00:11:20,147 --> 00:11:22,750
JOE SURE SEEMED BOTHERED
BY THIS THING.

228
00:11:22,783 --> 00:11:24,318
HOW DID HE CALL IT?

229
00:11:24,352 --> 00:11:26,987
YOU RECOGNIZED THE TERM HE USED.
I COULD TELL.

230
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:28,288
LOOK, I'LL EXPLAIN IT LATER,
NATALIE.

231
00:11:28,322 --> 00:11:29,590
GET SOME OF
THE STUDENTS OVER HERE

232
00:11:29,623 --> 00:11:31,158
TO TAKE THESE BONES
OUT OF HERE.

233
00:11:31,192 --> 00:11:34,162
DON'T PUT IT IN THE LAB TENT,
BRING IT UP TO THE...

234
00:11:34,195 --> 00:11:36,663
- AND NATALIE...
- NAALDLOOSHII, BABY.

235
00:11:36,697 --> 00:11:38,965
YOU MAKE SURE NONE
OF THE INDIAN WORKERS SEE THIS.

236
00:11:38,998 --> 00:11:44,205
- LIKE, UH, RAJIPUR
OR AMIR, OKAY?
- MAKE SURE.

237
00:11:44,238 --> 00:11:47,207
GOODBYE, JOE!

238
00:11:50,677 --> 00:11:55,582
OH, COULD YOU AT LEAST
PUT GYM SHORTS ON HIM?

239
00:11:55,615 --> 00:12:00,053
♪ AVE MARIA ♪

240
00:12:00,087 --> 00:12:04,892
WE'VE COME TO THE CONCLUSION,
DEM BONES, DEM DRY BONES, SIR.

241
00:12:04,925 --> 00:12:08,228
- SKIN-WALKER?
- SKIN-WALKER.

242
00:12:08,262 --> 00:12:10,130
TEXAS SKIN-RANGER.

243
00:12:10,163 --> 00:12:12,433
IT'S ALSO KNOWN
AS A SHAPE-SHIFTER.

244
00:12:12,467 --> 00:12:14,502
POT-STICKER, CLAM DIGGER,
THAT SORT OF THING.

245
00:12:14,535 --> 00:12:17,103
- IT'S THE NAVAJO EQUIVALENT
OF A, UH...

246
00:12:17,137 --> 00:12:20,573
- POODLE.

247
00:12:20,607 --> 00:12:23,110
LICHENTHROPE.

248
00:12:23,143 --> 00:12:25,645
A [...]DAMN WEREWOLF!

249
00:12:25,678 --> 00:12:28,615
A WHAT WEREWOLF?

250
00:12:28,648 --> 00:12:31,052
HERE'S THE WIND UP...
AND THE PITCH.

251
00:12:31,085 --> 00:12:34,888
- WEREWOLF?
- NO. WEREWOLF. WEAR. SAY IT.

252
00:12:34,922 --> 00:12:37,558
YOU MEAN, JOE THINKS
THIS THING IS A WEREWOLF?

253
00:12:37,592 --> 00:12:40,093
WELL, NOT EXACTLY.
NOT IN OUR TRADITIONAL

254
00:12:40,127 --> 00:12:43,197
WHITE MAN'S
MOVIE-MONSTER SENSE.

255
00:12:43,230 --> 00:12:45,598
YOU SEE,
NAALDLOOSHII TRANSLATED,

256
00:12:45,632 --> 00:12:48,102
MEANS "HE WHO TROTS
HERE AND THERE ON ALL FOURS."

257
00:12:48,135 --> 00:12:49,803
SO ANY ANIMAL, PRETTY MUCH.

258
00:12:49,837 --> 00:12:51,738
YOU KNOW WHAT,
LET ME EXPLAIN.

259
00:12:51,772 --> 00:12:55,142
A NAALDLOOSHII
IS A HUMAN WITCH

260
00:12:55,175 --> 00:12:57,778
WHO WEARS THE SKINS
OF FIERCE ANIMALS...

261
00:12:57,778 --> 00:13:00,113
SUCH AS A COYOTE,
OR WOLF, OR BEAR.

262
00:13:00,147 --> 00:13:01,282
RABBIT, CATERPILLAR,
YOU KNOW.

263
00:13:01,315 --> 00:13:03,717
HE ASSUMES THE QUALITY
OF THOSE ANIMALS.

264
00:13:03,750 --> 00:13:06,487
GAINS POWER FROM THEM.

265
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:08,088
HE'S BEEN KNOWN
TO ROAM ABOUT AT NIGHT

266
00:13:08,122 --> 00:13:11,358
CREATING ALL SORTS
OF MALEVOLENT DEEDS.

267
00:13:11,392 --> 00:13:13,327
THE NAVAJO CLAIM
THAT THEY CAN TELL

268
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,628
WHEN A NAALDLOOSHII IS CLOSE

269
00:13:14,662 --> 00:13:18,265
BY THE SUDDEN SOUND
OF ALL KINDS OF PECULIAR NOISES,

270
00:13:18,298 --> 00:13:20,100
AND PARTICULARLY,
THE LOUD BARKING OF DOGS.

271
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:22,235
MIGHT JUST BE
THE BUMPUSES' DOGS.
WE'RE NOT SURE.

272
00:13:22,268 --> 00:13:24,772
THEY ALSO CAN TELL
WHEN A MAN IS NAALDLOOSHII.

273
00:13:24,805 --> 00:13:27,942
HE TAKES ON A SERIES
OF STRANGE BODY HABITS.

274
00:13:27,975 --> 00:13:29,277
WEARS TOAST IN HIS PANTS.

275
00:13:29,310 --> 00:13:31,512
LIKE SLEEPING LIKE A COYOTE,
NOSE TO ANUS.

276
00:13:31,545 --> 00:13:35,182
- WHAT? IT'S FUN!
- NOW IT'S BEGINNING TO SMELL
OF COYOTE URINE.

277
00:13:37,317 --> 00:13:39,187
THIS IS ABSOLUTELY
FASCINATING.

278
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:40,720
- [CHUCKLING]
- RIGHT.

279
00:13:40,753 --> 00:13:42,823
♪♪

280
00:13:47,862 --> 00:13:49,930
SO HOW DO THEY STOP THEM?

281
00:13:49,963 --> 00:13:52,265
DID YOU HEAR THAT?

282
00:13:52,265 --> 00:13:55,068
IF I REMEMBER CORRECTLY,
THEY CALL IT A HATAALI.

283
00:13:55,102 --> 00:13:57,503
HE'S A MEDICINE MAN
PROTECT THEM.

284
00:13:57,538 --> 00:14:00,773
THE HATAALI COME IN
TO TRY TO--

285
00:14:00,807 --> 00:14:03,210
TO TRY TO GET
THE NAALDLOOSHII.

286
00:14:03,243 --> 00:14:04,912
USING HOOCHI-COOCHIE
HIKI-BLOCKY.

287
00:14:04,945 --> 00:14:06,713
- BUT IF HE'S TOO LATE,
- [DOG BARKS]

288
00:14:06,747 --> 00:14:09,617
THEY ARM THEMSELVES
AND THEY HUNT THE BASTARD DOWN.

289
00:14:09,650 --> 00:14:10,850
[HOWLING]

290
00:14:10,885 --> 00:14:12,318
OKAY, IS THAT A CUT?
YOU GET EVERYTHING?

291
00:14:12,352 --> 00:14:15,022
- LISTEN.
- IT'S ABSOLUTELY FASCINATING.

292
00:14:15,055 --> 00:14:16,357
WHAT WAS THAT?

293
00:14:16,390 --> 00:14:18,825
OH, I HAVE SMALL DOGS
IN MY HAIR. SORRY.

294
00:14:18,858 --> 00:14:20,360
PROBABLY CAR ON THE ROAD.

295
00:14:20,393 --> 00:14:23,963
YEAH, IT'S ONE OF THOSE CARS
THAT SOUNDS LIKE A WOLF, OKAY?

296
00:14:23,997 --> 00:14:28,202
ANYWAY, THAT'S WHAT I KNOW ABOUT
THE LEGEND OF THE NAALDLOOSHII.

297
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:35,008
♪♪ [SINGING]

298
00:14:35,042 --> 00:14:37,477
PURE MOODS.

299
00:14:37,510 --> 00:14:41,415
CAN I BE IN THE MOVIE AGAIN?

300
00:14:41,448 --> 00:14:43,883
AH, THEY JUST HEARD
THAT SAWYER BROWN BROKE UP.

301
00:14:43,917 --> 00:14:46,687
OH, HONEY.

302
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:48,488
HE'S WINNIE THE POOH.

303
00:14:48,522 --> 00:14:51,525
[CHUCKLES]

304
00:14:51,558 --> 00:14:56,997
I'M SORRY I BROKE
YOUR HANSON TAPE.

305
00:14:57,030 --> 00:15:00,400
DO YOU HAVE ANY SPARE ROLES
THAT I COULD DO?

306
00:15:00,433 --> 00:15:01,868
WELL, WHAT TOOK YOU SO LONG?

307
00:15:01,902 --> 00:15:03,437
THEY HAD TO STITCH HIM UP.

308
00:15:03,470 --> 00:15:06,373
- WELL, I MADE SUPPER.
- HOW IS HE?

309
00:15:06,407 --> 00:15:10,543
- HE'S BAD.
- HOW BAD?

310
00:15:10,577 --> 00:15:15,348
BAD-BAD.
- BAD-BAD-BAD
OR JUST BAD-BAD-BAD?

311
00:15:15,382 --> 00:15:19,553
I HEARD IT IN A LOVE SONG.
GOTTA GO.

312
00:15:19,587 --> 00:15:21,255
I'M STILL IN THIS MOVIE,
YOU KNOW.

313
00:15:21,288 --> 00:15:24,958
YOU MIGHT NOT THINK I AM,
BUT I AM!

314
00:15:24,992 --> 00:15:29,262
[SOBS]
I JUST HEARD
"GOODBYE ENGLAND'S ROSE."

315
00:15:31,732 --> 00:15:33,000
TIM BROKE UP WITH ME.

316
00:15:33,033 --> 00:15:36,770
WE WERE SUPPOSED TO GO
TO THAT WEDDING TOGETHER.

317
00:15:36,837 --> 00:15:39,573
DID HE LEAVE RIGHT IN THE MIDDLE
OF HIS PERM?

318
00:15:39,573 --> 00:15:40,673
CALL AN AMBULANCE.

319
00:15:40,707 --> 00:15:43,777
♪ CAN'T BE WRONG ♪

320
00:15:43,810 --> 00:15:45,545
WHAT?

321
00:15:45,578 --> 00:15:47,513
I SAID CALL AN AMBULANCE!

322
00:15:47,547 --> 00:15:48,848
WELL, I'M NOT
SUPPOSED TO LISTEN

323
00:15:48,882 --> 00:15:51,452
TO PEOPLE WHO AREN'T
IN THE MOVIE, BUT...

324
00:15:51,485 --> 00:15:53,253
CHIA ESTEVEZ.

325
00:15:53,287 --> 00:15:57,725
OH... [MUTED]

326
00:15:57,758 --> 00:16:03,330
WHAT ARE YOU STILL DOING
IN THIS MOVIE.

327
00:16:03,363 --> 00:16:07,233
- OH, TOMMY.
- HE LOOKS LIKE A PUFFED UP
ROUGH GROUSE.

328
00:16:09,002 --> 00:16:11,905
AND THE LITTER ON THE HIGHWAY.
IT'S JUST EVERYTHING.

329
00:16:11,938 --> 00:16:15,342
- LOOK, NOEL,
I'M NOT SUPERSTITIOUS.
- I'M STUPID.

330
00:16:15,375 --> 00:16:17,678
THIS REALLY ISN'T ANY KIND
OF CONVENTIONAL ANIMAL

331
00:16:17,712 --> 00:16:18,978
I'M FAMILIAR WITH.

332
00:16:19,012 --> 00:16:21,615
- IT'S NOT A BUNNY.
- WHAT DO YOU THINK IT IS?

333
00:16:21,648 --> 00:16:23,950
NATALIE, I REALLY COULDN'T
TELL YOU WHAT THIS THING IS.

334
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:28,422
- [MUMBLING]
- LOOK AT THE TEETH CLOSELY.

335
00:16:28,455 --> 00:16:31,825
- THIS THING RAN OFF,
MOVES LIKE A DOG.
- [MUMBLING]

336
00:16:31,858 --> 00:16:34,762
THE TEETH
ARE CANINE IN STRUCTURE,

337
00:16:34,795 --> 00:16:36,330
YET IT HAS HUMAN QUALITIES.

338
00:16:36,363 --> 00:16:40,600
WE'RE GONNA HAVE TO TAKE IT
BACK TO THE LAB AND STUDY IT.

339
00:16:40,633 --> 00:16:42,335
BUT AT THE RISK
OF SOUNDING NUTS...

340
00:16:42,368 --> 00:16:44,003
I'VE REPLACE MY TOES
WITH GRAPES.

341
00:16:44,037 --> 00:16:47,373
I THINK WE JUST STUMBLED ON
THE REMAINS OF A LICHENTHROPE.

342
00:16:47,407 --> 00:16:50,777
COME ON, NOEL.
YOU'RE A RATIONAL MAN.

343
00:16:50,810 --> 00:16:52,813
THAT'S IMPOSSIBLE.
WEREWOLVES?

344
00:16:52,847 --> 00:16:54,180
A SKIN-WALKER ISN'T?

345
00:16:54,213 --> 00:16:57,050
DON'T BE SO QUICK
TO DISMISS LEGENDS.

346
00:16:57,083 --> 00:16:58,585
LEGENDS HAVE TO BEGIN
SOMEWHERE.

347
00:16:58,618 --> 00:17:00,420
LIKE THE KEEBLER ELVES.

348
00:17:00,453 --> 00:17:02,655
PERHAPS THIS IS
A CREATURE OF LEGEND.

349
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:04,257
DO YOU REALIZE
IF THIS WAS A LICHENTHROPE...

350
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:06,827
I'D HAVE TO LOOK THE WORD UP.

351
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:09,830
IT COULD BE THE DISCOVERY
OF THE CENTURY.

352
00:17:09,863 --> 00:17:12,065
AND, NOT TO MENTION,
THE PERSON RESPONSIBLE

353
00:17:12,098 --> 00:17:15,368
FOR ITS DISCOVERY
WOULD BE FAMOUS!

354
00:17:15,402 --> 00:17:18,405
SO THEY HIRE
THE FRITO BANDITO.

355
00:17:18,438 --> 00:17:20,440
HEY LOOK,
IT'S CROW T. WEREWOLF.

356
00:17:20,473 --> 00:17:24,645
HEY.

357
00:17:24,678 --> 00:17:27,080
- [HOWLING]
- AH YES, THE CONCERTO

358
00:17:27,113 --> 00:17:32,152
IN A-MINOR
FOR CELLO AND WEREWOLF.

359
00:17:32,185 --> 00:17:34,755
OKAY. GOD,
THEY'RE ESTABLISHING

360
00:17:34,788 --> 00:17:36,257
THE HELL OUT OF
THIS BUILDING HERE.

361
00:17:36,290 --> 00:17:37,758
[CHUCKLES]
YEAH.

362
00:17:37,792 --> 00:17:39,660
- [HOWLING CONTINUES]
- OKAY.

363
00:17:39,693 --> 00:17:42,362
THE SHEET HAS NO PULSE.

364
00:17:42,395 --> 00:17:47,133
HIS CONDITION HAS GONE
TO BAD-BAD-BAD-BAD-BAD-BAD.

365
00:17:47,167 --> 00:17:50,870
I'M AFRAID HE'S OPENED
TOO MANY CASINOS.

366
00:17:55,775 --> 00:17:58,812
DID HE SEEM, YOU KNOW,
UH, DEAD TO YOU?

367
00:17:58,845 --> 00:18:02,482
DOCTOR, WHAT DO YOU THINK?

368
00:18:02,515 --> 00:18:04,150
WELL, I CAN'T MAKE IT OUT.

369
00:18:04,183 --> 00:18:06,987
I'VE NEVER SEEN
A CASE LIKE THIS BEFORE.

370
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:10,190
- I MEAN, YOU SAW HIS FACE.
- YES, I DID.

371
00:18:10,223 --> 00:18:12,758
THERE IS CONSTANT
TRANSFORMATION.

372
00:18:12,793 --> 00:18:15,328
WHAT SHOULD WE DO?
SHOULD WE CALL DR. BROWN?

373
00:18:15,362 --> 00:18:16,663
NO, THAT'S NOT NECESSARY.

374
00:18:16,697 --> 00:18:19,165
JUST GET A BLOOD TEST,
SEND IT TO THE LAB.

375
00:18:19,232 --> 00:18:21,935
AND KEEP HIM
UNDER INTENSE OBSERVATION.

376
00:18:21,968 --> 00:18:23,637
YES, DOCTOR.

377
00:18:23,670 --> 00:18:26,307
NOW YOU SHOULD GET SOME REST.
YOU LOOK EXHAUSTED.

378
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:27,640
YEAH, WELL WHAT ABOUT
YOUR ROOTS?

379
00:18:27,673 --> 00:18:31,010
YEAH, THANK YOU
FOR THE ADVICE.

380
00:18:31,043 --> 00:18:33,013
I QUESTIONED GLUING
CREPE HAIR TO HIS FACE, NURSE,

381
00:18:33,047 --> 00:18:38,252
BUT YOU SEEM TO KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE DOING.

382
00:18:38,285 --> 00:18:40,253
HE'S GOING TO HAVE TO WEAR
ONE OF THOSE CONES

383
00:18:40,287 --> 00:18:43,223
AROUND HIS NECK NOW.

384
00:18:43,257 --> 00:18:47,828
I ADMIRE
YOUR HAIR-HELMET, SIR.

385
00:18:47,862 --> 00:18:52,032
AH, I'M GONNA PULL THE PLUG,
JUST FOR THE HELL OF IT.

386
00:18:52,065 --> 00:18:55,435
- TIME TO DO A JENNY GARP.
- OH, YEAH.

387
00:18:58,172 --> 00:18:59,707
UM, I HAVE BAD NEWS,

388
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:02,742
WE HAVE TO REMOVE
YOUR CONTINENT.

389
00:19:06,247 --> 00:19:11,252
SO YOU WANT TO FIGHT, OR...

390
00:19:11,285 --> 00:19:16,290
THE FORD RANGER,
THE OFFICIAL TRUCK
OF THE ENGLISH PATIENT.

391
00:19:16,323 --> 00:19:19,793
MAN, IT WAS LUCKY
TO FIND THIS PARKING SPACE.

392
00:19:22,897 --> 00:19:24,397
HIS HAIR'S
COMPLETELY DIFFERENT.

393
00:19:24,430 --> 00:19:26,233
- YEAH.
- WHERE IN THE HELL
HAVE YOU BEEN?

394
00:19:26,267 --> 00:19:27,968
DO YOU KNOW
WHAT TIME IT IS?

395
00:19:28,002 --> 00:19:30,970
WHERE IN THE HELL IS TOMMY?

396
00:19:31,003 --> 00:19:33,973
[MUTED], HERE WE GO AGAIN.

397
00:19:34,007 --> 00:19:38,245
AH, NOTHING LIKE A WARM V8.

398
00:19:38,278 --> 00:19:40,680
HEY, I'M TALKING TO YOU!

399
00:19:40,713 --> 00:19:42,148
- [CHUCKLES]
- AND?

400
00:19:42,182 --> 00:19:44,350
TOMMY'S AT
CITY EMERGENCY HOSPITAL.

401
00:19:44,383 --> 00:19:46,152
HE'S SICK!

402
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:47,287
- THE GUY'S TURNING INTO--
- SHH!

403
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:48,755
HONEY, SHH.

404
00:19:48,788 --> 00:19:50,390
HE'S REAL SICK.

405
00:19:50,423 --> 00:19:52,325
WHAT'S WRONG WITH HIM?

406
00:19:52,358 --> 00:19:53,827
HE GOT AN INFECTION
FROM THAT THING

407
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:56,463
HE CUT HIMSELF ON YESTERDAY.

408
00:19:56,497 --> 00:19:57,730
THAT'S ALL I KNOW.

409
00:19:57,763 --> 00:19:59,398
FOUNTAIN O' HAIR.

410
00:19:59,432 --> 00:20:03,537
NOW, IF YOU DON'T MIND,
I'D LIKE TO GO BACK TO WORK.

411
00:20:03,570 --> 00:20:05,772
GOOD.

412
00:20:05,838 --> 00:20:08,675
THIS IS GONNA BE A FUN DIG.

413
00:20:11,645 --> 00:20:14,982
HEY, LOOK!
AN ANCIENT BEER CAN! OH...

414
00:20:18,285 --> 00:20:20,987
IS HE DRAINING HIS EARS
INTO HIS POCKET?

415
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:23,523
I'VE GONE BACK TO MY DARKER,
SHORTER HAIR NOW.

416
00:20:23,557 --> 00:20:25,225
[BABY CRYING]

417
00:20:25,258 --> 00:20:28,662
SO THEY PUT SUSPECTED WEREWOLVES
IN THE NEONATAL UNIT, HUH.

418
00:20:31,465 --> 00:20:35,735
- MAN, INFANTS ARE SUCH BABIES.
- YEAH.

419
00:20:35,768 --> 00:20:39,238
MAN, HE MAKES TED DANSON
LOOK LIKE GAVIN MCCLOUD.

420
00:20:41,642 --> 00:20:43,010
YES, I AM A DOCTOR.

421
00:20:43,043 --> 00:20:45,912
I'LL JUST BE BEING DOCTOR
IN HERE THEN.

422
00:20:45,945 --> 00:20:49,683
DOCTOR, THAT'S ME.

423
00:20:49,717 --> 00:20:54,087
ALL RIGHTY THEN,
A COMPLETE DESANGUINATION
FOR YOU THEN?

424
00:20:55,488 --> 00:20:56,990
OKAY, WE'LL BE TRANSFERRING YOU

425
00:20:57,023 --> 00:21:01,628
TO THE HO-CHUNK HOSPITAL
FOR NAALDLOOSHIIS.

426
00:21:01,628 --> 00:21:04,530
EXCUSE ME,
WHERE'S YOUR HEADPHONE JACK?

427
00:21:08,735 --> 00:21:12,038
AUDIENCE,
WHAT'S YOUR DIAGNOSIS?

428
00:21:15,942 --> 00:21:18,078
HERE, SOME LITTER I PICKED UP
OFF THE FREEWAY.

429
00:21:18,112 --> 00:21:20,213
DOES THAT
MAKE YOU FEEL BETTER?

430
00:21:23,917 --> 00:21:27,720
NO, NO, NO, I DON'T THINK
THIS CASE CALLS FOR MINOXIDIL.

431
00:21:29,690 --> 00:21:33,393
OH, SORRY, I THOUGHT
YOU WERE ROBERT DOWNEY JR.

432
00:21:34,928 --> 00:21:36,430
WHAT AM I DOING?
I'M NOT A D--

433
00:21:36,463 --> 00:21:38,932
I MUST HAVE PANICKED
AND THOUGHT I WAS A DOCTOR.

434
00:21:38,965 --> 00:21:41,435
PANICKED.

435
00:21:44,203 --> 00:21:47,807
♪ EE-O-ELEVEN ♪

436
00:21:50,677 --> 00:21:54,682
WELL, I BETTER GET BACK
TO MY BRUCE JENNER SHIFT.

437
00:21:59,118 --> 00:22:00,320
SNAUSAGES.

438
00:22:00,353 --> 00:22:02,922
SNAU-SNAUSAGES.

439
00:22:02,955 --> 00:22:05,358
AS A RECUPERATING WEREWOLF,
I'M VERY PLEASED

440
00:22:05,392 --> 00:22:10,063
WITH MY CRAFTMATIC
ADJUSTABLE BED.

441
00:22:10,097 --> 00:22:13,100
OH, I ATE TOO MUCH.
I AM A FULL MOON.

442
00:22:13,133 --> 00:22:15,968
- [LAUGHTER]
- I AM GONNA HIT YOU SO...

443
00:22:16,002 --> 00:22:20,940
SOMEONE'S TRYING TO START
THEIR PLYMOUTH DUSTER.

444
00:22:20,973 --> 00:22:23,477
WELL, IT'S EITHER
ASHFORD OR SIMPSON.

445
00:22:23,510 --> 00:22:25,745
QUICK,
APPLY INTRAVENOUS NAIR!

446
00:22:25,778 --> 00:22:30,283
[HOWLS]

447
00:22:30,317 --> 00:22:33,853
LET ME JUST CHILL MY HANDS
AND I'LL BE RIGHT THERE.

448
00:22:35,755 --> 00:22:38,892
- [SNARLS]
- [SCREAMS]

449
00:22:38,925 --> 00:22:43,463
WEREWOLF CAN KIND OF
SLIP ON HIS JEANS.

450
00:22:43,497 --> 00:22:44,965
NOT BOB VILA! NO!

451
00:22:44,998 --> 00:22:47,667
NOW, WHAT WE'RE DOING HERE, BOB,
IS GETTING KILLED BY A WEREWOLF.

452
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:50,637
[SHOUTING]

453
00:22:50,670 --> 00:22:54,908
LATER, IN THE DEAD
OF BLUE-FILTER NIGHT.

454
00:22:54,942 --> 00:22:58,745
MAYBE THE ICE-CREAM TRUCK
JUST ISN'T COMING TODAY.

455
00:22:58,778 --> 00:23:01,280
- WHAT DO YOU GOT THERE?
- SILVER BULLET.

456
00:23:01,313 --> 00:23:03,517
THERE'S COORS LIGHT
IN YOUR GUN?

457
00:23:03,550 --> 00:23:04,785
ME TOO.

458
00:23:04,818 --> 00:23:07,520
THIS WILL TAKE CARE OF HIM.

459
00:23:07,553 --> 00:23:11,758
WHAT MAKES YOU THINK
HE'S GONNA COME BACK HERE?

460
00:23:11,792 --> 00:23:14,327
EVERYBODY'S OUT
LOOKING FOR HIM, RIGHT?

461
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:17,330
YEAH.

462
00:23:17,363 --> 00:23:19,065
WHERE YOU THINK
HE'S GONNA COME BACK TO?

463
00:23:19,098 --> 00:23:21,400
WELL, THE COUCH ON THE PORCH
IS BASICALLY HIS.

464
00:23:21,435 --> 00:23:23,170
BACK TO HIS LAIR.

465
00:23:23,203 --> 00:23:25,405
WE'LL BE READY FOR HIM.

466
00:23:28,073 --> 00:23:30,710
- [SNARLS]
- AH, WHAT? HE BECAME A BAT?

467
00:23:30,743 --> 00:23:32,545
A BUG? WHAT IS THAT?

468
00:23:32,578 --> 00:23:36,082
LOOK. I SEE SOMETHING
OVER THERE.

469
00:23:36,115 --> 00:23:38,985
IT'S A GUY
WITH A WOLF HAND-PUPPET!

470
00:23:43,723 --> 00:23:45,692
THAT'S HIM.

471
00:23:45,725 --> 00:23:49,162
GO AND USE THE BATHROOM
BEFORE WE LEAVE.

472
00:23:49,195 --> 00:23:50,163
♪♪ [NATIVE AMERICAN DRUMMING]

473
00:23:50,197 --> 00:23:52,898
HUH, THE NATIVES
ARE CLOSING IN.

474
00:23:55,335 --> 00:23:56,803
UM, IF IT'S MARTIN,
SHOOT TO KILL.

475
00:23:56,837 --> 00:23:59,372
THEN I CAN BE IN SPAWN.

476
00:24:00,907 --> 00:24:03,677
- [GROWLING]
- WAIT! IT'S A GORILLA!

477
00:24:03,710 --> 00:24:06,145
WITH A DOG MASK ON.

478
00:24:09,082 --> 00:24:12,285
SOMEHOW JANET RENO'S
BEHIND THIS.

479
00:24:13,353 --> 00:24:16,255
- [SNARLING]
- [GUN SHOT]

480
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,723
BEN!

481
00:24:17,757 --> 00:24:21,160
THE LEAST SUCCESSFUL WEREWOLF
OF ALL TIME.

482
00:24:21,193 --> 00:24:22,828
WHAT A LAME WEREWOLF.

483
00:24:22,862 --> 00:24:25,932
[WHIMPERING]

484
00:24:39,913 --> 00:24:42,882
BOY, THAT JOE ESTEVEZ
IS ONE COMPELLING PERFORMER.

485
00:24:42,915 --> 00:24:45,652
HE'S REALLY LIGHTING UP
THE SCREEN, I TELL YOU.

486
00:24:45,685 --> 00:24:48,255
HE COULD REALLY SHOW
HIS BROTHER MARTIN SHEEN

487
00:24:48,288 --> 00:24:49,522
A THING OR TWO ABOUT ACTING.

488
00:24:49,555 --> 00:24:51,992
I'M SURE GLAD HE'S IN
THIS WEREWOLF MOVIE.

489
00:24:52,025 --> 00:24:53,260
- YEAH.
- YEAH.

490
00:24:53,293 --> 00:24:55,428
OH, WHICH REMINDS ME,
DID YOU GUYS HAVE ANY TIME

491
00:24:55,462 --> 00:24:56,697
TO THINK ABOUT WHAT I ASKED?

492
00:24:56,730 --> 00:24:59,065
YOU KNOW, WHO WOULD YOU WANT
IN YOUR WEREWOLF MOVIE?

493
00:24:59,098 --> 00:25:03,002
UH, SURE, MIKE.
BUT, UH, WHY DON'T YOU GO FIRST?

494
00:25:03,035 --> 00:25:04,337
OH, SURE. OKAY.

495
00:25:04,370 --> 00:25:06,138
WELL, UH, FIRST OFF,
I THINK I WOULD HAVE

496
00:25:06,172 --> 00:25:08,208
BURT REYNOLDS' BROTHER
TIM REYNOLDS.

497
00:25:08,242 --> 00:25:09,943
- AH.
- YOU KNOW, IF THAT
DIDN'T WORK OUT,

498
00:25:09,977 --> 00:25:12,478
I WOULD-- I WOULD GO FOR
EMILIO KLUGMAN.

499
00:25:12,512 --> 00:25:13,480
- SURE.
- UH-HUH.

500
00:25:13,513 --> 00:25:15,782
AND, UH, MAYBE AS A ROLE
AS A BIKER

501
00:25:15,815 --> 00:25:17,383
OR SOMETHING LIKE THAT,
I WOULD GO FOR

502
00:25:17,417 --> 00:25:19,852
DON KNOTTS' TOUGHER BROTHER
SPIKE KNOTTS.

503
00:25:19,887 --> 00:25:21,220
- OOH.
- AH, GOOD IDEA.

504
00:25:21,253 --> 00:25:22,922
- SERVO?
- AH, THANKS, MIKE.

505
00:25:22,955 --> 00:25:25,225
WELL, I PLAYED
BY A SLIGHTLY MORE FREESTYLE

506
00:25:25,258 --> 00:25:26,560
SET OF RULES THAN YOU, MIKE.

507
00:25:26,593 --> 00:25:29,028
TO WHICH, MY FIRST CHOICE
IN MY WEREWOLF MOVIE

508
00:25:29,095 --> 00:25:32,465
WOULD BE ONE MR. SAMMY HATCH,
BROTHER OF SENATOR ORRIN.

509
00:25:32,498 --> 00:25:34,033
- YEAH.
- THEN I'D CERTAINLY GO FOR

510
00:25:34,067 --> 00:25:35,968
MICHAEL DEBAKEY'S BROTHER
JAKE DEBAKEY.

511
00:25:36,002 --> 00:25:38,505
- MM-HMM.
- OR LOUIS PASTEUR'S
BROTHER GREG.

512
00:25:38,538 --> 00:25:40,773
ALAS, NO LONGER
IN THIS MORTAL COIL,

513
00:25:40,807 --> 00:25:42,442
BUT A GREAT CHOICE
FOR MY WEREWOLF MOVIE.

514
00:25:42,475 --> 00:25:44,810
OR, UM, CHIP HITLER.

515
00:25:44,843 --> 00:25:46,512
- YEAH, SURE, THAT'S, UH--
- CHIP HITLER.

516
00:25:46,545 --> 00:25:48,648
YOU KNOW, I ADMIRE
YOUR FREEWHEELING STYLE.

517
00:25:48,682 --> 00:25:51,150
IT REALLY OPENED UP
THE POSSIBILITIES.

518
00:25:51,183 --> 00:25:53,287
- THANKS, MIKE.
- CROW?

519
00:25:53,320 --> 00:25:55,288
WHO WOULD YOU WANT
IN YOUR WEREWOLF MOVIE?

520
00:25:55,322 --> 00:25:57,323
UH, YOU KNOW,
I DON'T KNOW, YOU GUYS.

521
00:25:57,357 --> 00:26:00,127
I TRIED, BUT FOR SOME REASON
ALL I COULD THINK OF

522
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:02,862
WAS RAY LIOTTA.
[SIGHS]

523
00:26:02,895 --> 00:26:04,130
- RAY LIOTTA?
- HUH.

524
00:26:04,163 --> 00:26:05,665
WELL, THAT'S WEIRD. I MEAN--

525
00:26:05,698 --> 00:26:07,900
WOULDN'T RATHER HAVE, LIKE,
RAY LIOTTA'S BROTHER, OR--

526
00:26:07,933 --> 00:26:09,835
UH, I DON'T KNOW.
I'M SORRY.

527
00:26:09,868 --> 00:26:11,605
I'M JUST NOT AS GOOD AT THIS
AS YOU GUYS.

528
00:26:11,638 --> 00:26:14,373
- I'M REALLY SORRY.
- JUST RAY LIOTTA, HUH?

529
00:26:14,407 --> 00:26:17,043
- DAMN. DAMN.
- WELL...

530
00:26:17,077 --> 00:26:18,445
DESPITE THAT LAST
AWKWARD MOMENT,

531
00:26:18,478 --> 00:26:20,813
I THINK
WE ALL ENJOYED PLAYING

532
00:26:20,847 --> 00:26:22,748
"WHO WOULD YOU WANT
IN YOUR WEREWOLF MOVIE?"

533
00:26:22,782 --> 00:26:25,985
[LAUGHS]
TRY IT AT HOME!

534
00:26:26,018 --> 00:26:28,220
IT'S FUN, YOU'LL SEE.

535
00:26:28,253 --> 00:26:29,788
GOODBYE.

536
00:26:29,822 --> 00:26:31,023
I DON'T KNOW YOU GUYS,

537
00:26:31,057 --> 00:26:32,692
I THINK RAY LIOTTA
WOULD MAKE AN OKAY WEREWOLF.

538
00:26:32,725 --> 00:26:35,128
- NO, HE SMELLS LIKE APPLES.
- OH, RIGHT, RIGHT, RIGHT.

539
00:26:35,162 --> 00:26:36,295
FOR CRYING OUT LOUD.

540
00:26:36,328 --> 00:26:38,230
♪♪

541
00:26:43,670 --> 00:26:46,038
- [LAUGHS]
- THAT WAS GOOD FUN.

542
00:26:46,072 --> 00:26:49,242
OH, TRAVIS BICKLE
MOVED OUT TO THE SUBURBS, HUH?

543
00:26:49,275 --> 00:26:54,313
HEY!
♪♪ [HUMS MORK & MINDY THEME]

544
00:26:54,347 --> 00:26:56,783
- MORK & MINDY.
- ALOHA, AND WELCOME TO HAWAII.

545
00:26:56,817 --> 00:27:00,587
THIS, OF COURSE,
IS THE PEARL HARBOR MEMORIAL.

546
00:27:04,557 --> 00:27:06,558
WHAT, ARE WE MOVING
INTO THIS HOUSE, SIR?

547
00:27:06,592 --> 00:27:09,262
- YEAH. WHY?
- JUST WONDERING.
I'M JUST CURIOUS, THAT'S ALL.

548
00:27:09,295 --> 00:27:11,932
- HOW MUCH DO I OWE YOU?
- UH, 15.

549
00:27:11,965 --> 00:27:14,133
- REALLY NICE OF YOU.
- GOOD LUCK.

550
00:27:14,167 --> 00:27:17,670
TURNS OUT THERE ARE SMALL PARTS
AND SMALL ACTORS.

551
00:27:17,703 --> 00:27:18,972
♪♪ [ATONAL PIANO]

552
00:27:19,005 --> 00:27:20,373
MAN, HOW DOES THE DIRECTOR
EVEN CONCEIVE

553
00:27:20,407 --> 00:27:24,343
OF THE FRAMING OF THIS SHOT?
IT'S JUST AMAZING.

554
00:27:24,377 --> 00:27:26,412
CAR OVER HERE
IN THE FOREGROUND.

555
00:27:26,445 --> 00:27:30,950
THE PIANO TUNER PUT HIS SPEAKERS
OUT THE WINDOW.

556
00:27:30,983 --> 00:27:34,420
[DOORBELL RINGS]

557
00:27:34,453 --> 00:27:36,222
DICTATOR FOR LIFE, SANTA.

558
00:27:36,255 --> 00:27:39,692
- HELLO?
- I'M PAUL.

559
00:27:43,095 --> 00:27:45,698
SORRY, I WAS JUST TAKING
A LAVENDER BATH.

560
00:27:45,732 --> 00:27:49,968
- PAUL WHO?
- PAUL NILES.

561
00:27:50,002 --> 00:27:52,605
OH, SURE.
[CHUCKLES]

562
00:27:52,638 --> 00:27:55,175
DOES THIS REALLY WARRANT
THE TENDER MUSIC?

563
00:27:55,208 --> 00:27:57,343
COME ON IN.
WE'RE EXPECTING YOU.

564
00:27:57,377 --> 00:27:59,145
WHY DON'T YOU HEAD DOWN
TO THE CRAWL-SPACE.

565
00:27:59,178 --> 00:28:00,647
I'LL BE RIGHT THERE
TO KILL YOU.

566
00:28:00,680 --> 00:28:02,482
[CHUCKLES]

567
00:28:02,515 --> 00:28:04,050
GLAD TO SEE
YOU COULD MAKE IT.

568
00:28:04,083 --> 00:28:09,488
DID YOU BRING YOUR
ANTI-GOVERNMENT PROPAGANDA?

569
00:28:09,522 --> 00:28:12,858
MISS CARRIE'S UPSTAIRS
WAITING FOR YOU.

570
00:28:12,892 --> 00:28:15,062
OH.

571
00:28:15,095 --> 00:28:18,163
WELL, I'VE GOT A SQUIRREL
IN THE OVEN IF YOU'RE HUNGRY.

572
00:28:18,197 --> 00:28:20,600
FIDEL CASTRO, HOUSE MOTHER.

573
00:28:20,633 --> 00:28:24,403
- I'M SAM.
- I'VE BEEN ISSUED
AS YOUR BEST FRIEND.

574
00:28:24,437 --> 00:28:27,407
I'M THE KEEPER.

575
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:29,608
- WELL, NICE TO MEET YOU.
- THE AVERAGE WHITE MAN.

576
00:28:29,642 --> 00:28:31,845
DO YOU ALWAYS GREET PEOPLE
WITH A GUN IN YOUR HAND?

577
00:28:31,878 --> 00:28:35,715
WHAT, THIS? THIS IS JUST
TO KEEP THE FLIES DOWN.

578
00:28:35,748 --> 00:28:38,217
THERE'S SOME WEIRD THINGS
HAPPENING AROUND HERE.

579
00:28:38,250 --> 00:28:42,422
THIS IS A STRANGE REMAKE
OF JANE EYRE.

580
00:28:42,455 --> 00:28:45,192
- MR. NILES.
- WE'RE SHARING A BED.

581
00:28:45,225 --> 00:28:49,662
I JUST FOUND OUT
COUNT DRACULA WAS A [MUTED].

582
00:28:49,695 --> 00:28:53,232
OH. IS THAT SO?

583
00:28:53,265 --> 00:28:55,335
YEAH, YOU DON'T
HAVE TO BELIEVE ME,

584
00:28:55,368 --> 00:28:57,537
BUT THAT'S THE FACTS.

585
00:28:57,570 --> 00:29:01,407
- SUDDENLY I MISS MY DAD.
- AH.

586
00:29:01,407 --> 00:29:04,077
HA!
♪ WEIRD THINGS A-GOIN' ♪

587
00:29:04,077 --> 00:29:05,945
♪ WEIRD THINGS A-COMIN' ♪

588
00:29:05,978 --> 00:29:09,515
♪ WEIRD THINGS A-DOIN'
AROUND HERE ♪

589
00:29:09,548 --> 00:29:10,817
[LAUGHTER]
OKAY.

590
00:29:10,850 --> 00:29:14,387
HEY! YUP, THE GRISLED
MILITIA MAN HAS A CHARMING B&B.

591
00:29:14,420 --> 00:29:16,990
[TYPEWRITER CLACKS]

592
00:29:17,023 --> 00:29:21,327
COME ON, THE SHELTERING SKY
MOVED QUICKER THAN THIS MOVIE.

593
00:29:21,360 --> 00:29:22,762
[GASPS]
OH, MY GOD.

594
00:29:22,795 --> 00:29:26,800
I DIDN'T HEAR YOU COME IN.

595
00:29:26,833 --> 00:29:29,702
HI, I'M PAUL NILES.
UH, SORRY IF I SCARED YOU.

596
00:29:29,735 --> 00:29:31,838
OF COURSE.

597
00:29:31,872 --> 00:29:34,573
I WAS JUST FINISHING
TYPING THIS NOTE FOR YOU.

598
00:29:34,607 --> 00:29:36,910
WELL, UH, READ IT.

599
00:29:36,943 --> 00:29:38,410
YOU MEAN THIS?

600
00:29:38,443 --> 00:29:40,747
DEAR SIR, SEND PANTS AT ONCE.

601
00:29:40,780 --> 00:29:43,817
DEAR MR. NILES,
I WAITED FOR YOU ALL DAY,

602
00:29:43,850 --> 00:29:45,718
BUT YOU DIDN'T SHOW UP.

603
00:29:45,752 --> 00:29:47,987
THEREFORE, I HAD TO GO
TO THE OFFICE.

604
00:29:48,020 --> 00:29:51,190
PLEASE CALL ME WHEN YOU GET IN.
CORDIALLY, CARRIE.

605
00:29:51,223 --> 00:29:55,995
WE'RE GONNA PASS ON YOUR LETTER.
GOOD LUCK, THOUGH.

606
00:29:56,062 --> 00:29:57,897
YEAH, MY FLIGHT WAS DELAYED
FROM NEW YORK,

607
00:29:57,897 --> 00:30:01,167
BUT, UH, THANKS ANYWAY.

608
00:30:01,200 --> 00:30:03,268
WELL, WHAT DO YOU THINK?

609
00:30:03,302 --> 00:30:06,205
PANTS OR NO PANTS?

610
00:30:06,238 --> 00:30:09,475
BEFORE YOUR MOTHER PASSED AWAY,
WE TRIED TO SELL THE HOUSE.

611
00:30:09,508 --> 00:30:11,077
BUT WITH THE RESTORATIONS
AND THE POOR ECONOMY,

612
00:30:11,110 --> 00:30:13,747
WE DIDN'T HAVE MANY OFFERS.

613
00:30:13,780 --> 00:30:15,113
WHEN I HEARD
YOU WERE COMING BACK,

614
00:30:15,147 --> 00:30:17,017
I THOUGHT I'D USE
THE LITTLE BUDGET I HAD

615
00:30:17,050 --> 00:30:18,818
TO FIX UP THE ATTIC.

616
00:30:18,852 --> 00:30:22,155
UNTIL YOU DECIDED
WHAT TO DO WITH THE HOUSE.

617
00:30:22,188 --> 00:30:24,590
WELL, THANKS TO YOU
IT'S REALLY NICE.

618
00:30:24,623 --> 00:30:28,327
IT'S THE PERFECT PLACE
FOR A STRUGGLING YOUNG WRITER.

619
00:30:28,360 --> 00:30:29,528
YOU KNOW WHAT,
I'M GONNA COME OVER THERE.

620
00:30:29,562 --> 00:30:30,930
I CAN'T HEAR YOU AT ALL.

621
00:30:30,963 --> 00:30:32,998
I CAN'T WAIT TO FIND OUT
WHAT YOUR BOOK'S ABOUT.

622
00:30:33,032 --> 00:30:34,700
JUST ANOTHER WINDOWS GUIDE.

623
00:30:34,733 --> 00:30:37,570
WELL, IT WAS A PLEASURE
MEETING YOU, CARRIE.

624
00:30:37,603 --> 00:30:40,773
WELL, I GUESS I BETTER GO
SO YOU CAN UNPACK.

625
00:30:40,807 --> 00:30:43,543
UH, DID YOU KNOW YOUR GRANDPA
SMELLS LIKE BEEFARONI?

626
00:30:43,577 --> 00:30:45,512
BY THE WAY, UH...

627
00:30:45,545 --> 00:30:47,713
WHO IS THAT GUY DOWNSTAIRS?

628
00:30:47,747 --> 00:30:49,515
OH, YOU MEAN SAM?

629
00:30:49,515 --> 00:30:51,283
I WOULDN'T WORRY ABOUT HIM.

630
00:30:51,350 --> 00:30:53,853
- HE'S JUST THE GROUNDSKEEPER.
- AND MURDERER.

631
00:30:53,887 --> 00:30:57,290
BY THE WAY, WHAT ARE
YOUR BIG PLANS FOR TONIGHT?

632
00:30:57,323 --> 00:30:59,558
PLANS?
I HAVEN'T GOT ANY. WHY?

633
00:30:59,592 --> 00:31:01,660
BECAUSE I WAS INVITED
TO A BIRTHDAY PARTY,

634
00:31:01,693 --> 00:31:03,730
AND I THOUGHT
YOU MIGHT LIKE TO COME.

635
00:31:03,763 --> 00:31:05,163
ARE YOU SURE
IT WOULDN'T BE AN INCONVENIENCE?

636
00:31:05,197 --> 00:31:06,900
I MEAN, I DON'T KNOW
ANYBODY THERE.

637
00:31:06,933 --> 00:31:09,035
YOU'LL GET TO KNOW THEM ALL.

638
00:31:09,068 --> 00:31:11,337
- IT'S A SMALL TOWN.
- IT IS?

639
00:31:11,370 --> 00:31:16,442
- I'LL PICK YOU UP AT 8:00.
- WEAR PANTS.

640
00:31:16,475 --> 00:31:17,977
IT'S "INCREDIBLE."

641
00:31:18,010 --> 00:31:21,247
HE'S A RENT-A-CENTER
ANDY GARCIA.

642
00:31:24,383 --> 00:31:26,452
AH, I SEE SOME REALLY
STUPID CHILDREN BEING BORN

643
00:31:26,485 --> 00:31:28,520
AS A RESULT
OF THESE TWO MEETING.

644
00:31:28,553 --> 00:31:31,257
WOW. OH, WOW.

645
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:39,532
WELL, I'M GLAD
WE HAD THAT MOMENT.

646
00:31:39,565 --> 00:31:43,068
HI, MINNIE PEARL.

647
00:31:43,102 --> 00:31:47,040
HEY, EVERYONE,
FREE SAMPLES OF ME.

648
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:49,708
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

649
00:31:49,742 --> 00:31:51,143
[CHATTER]

650
00:31:51,177 --> 00:31:54,047
I COULDN'T HELP NOTICING
YOU WEREN'T HAVING SEX WITH ME.

651
00:31:54,080 --> 00:31:57,183
EXCUSE ME PLEASE.

652
00:31:57,217 --> 00:31:59,518
YOU LOOK
SO BEAUTIFUL TONIGHT.

653
00:31:59,552 --> 00:32:02,022
UH, THANK YOU, YURI.
THAT'S VERY NICE OF YOU TO SAY.

654
00:32:02,055 --> 00:32:04,257
- NOW, UM--
- YOU KNOW, YOU'RE A KNOCKOUT.

655
00:32:04,290 --> 00:32:05,758
WILL YOU EXCUSE ME
FOR A MINUTE?

656
00:32:05,792 --> 00:32:08,327
- I SEE SOMEBODY.
- WHO'S NOT A SERIAL KILLER.

657
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:10,730
COME HERE. DON'T GO.

658
00:32:10,763 --> 00:32:12,765
HOW ABOUT A LITTLE KISS?
HOW ABOUT IT?

659
00:32:12,798 --> 00:32:14,800
NO, NO, YURI.
THIS IS A PARTY. PLEASE.

660
00:32:14,833 --> 00:32:16,235
OH, BABY, YOU LOOK SO GOOD.

661
00:32:16,268 --> 00:32:18,003
AND THIS IS
MY REAL GOOD FRIEND, ELGIN.

662
00:32:18,037 --> 00:32:19,705
- ELGIN, GOOD TO MEET YOU.
- GOOD MEETING YOU.

663
00:32:19,738 --> 00:32:21,007
ELGIN'S MY BLACK FRIEND.

664
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:24,377
- WHY?
- LOOK, ISN'T THAT MUSIC
BEAUTIFUL?

665
00:32:24,410 --> 00:32:26,578
I THINK
THE LADY SAID NO, HUH?

666
00:32:26,612 --> 00:32:28,782
HEY! TAKE YOUR HANDS OFF ME.

667
00:32:28,815 --> 00:32:30,048
LET GO OF ME NOW!

668
00:32:30,082 --> 00:32:31,317
AND LOUD MUMBLING BREAKS OUT.

669
00:32:31,350 --> 00:32:34,220
[INDISTINCT MUMBLING]

670
00:32:34,253 --> 00:32:35,522
UH, MOVIE,
IS THERE'S SOMETHING

671
00:32:35,522 --> 00:32:37,257
YOU'D LIKE TO SHARE
WITH THE REST OF US?

672
00:32:37,290 --> 00:32:39,525
COME ON.

673
00:32:39,558 --> 00:32:42,495
NOW, LET A REAL MAN
LOOK DOWN YOUR BLOUSE.

674
00:32:42,528 --> 00:32:44,197
LOOK, YURI.

675
00:32:44,230 --> 00:32:45,230
WHAT THE HELL
IS WRONG WITH YOU?

676
00:32:45,263 --> 00:32:46,598
YOU ARE MARRIED TO ME.

677
00:32:46,632 --> 00:32:48,735
I SUGGEST YOU STAY OUT HERE
AND GET SOBER

678
00:32:48,768 --> 00:32:50,235
BEFORE YOU REJOIN THE PARTY.

679
00:32:50,268 --> 00:32:53,405
AND WHEN YOU DO,
YOU CAN APOLOGIZE TO NATALIE.

680
00:32:53,438 --> 00:32:57,077
- NOW GO TAKE A WALK.
- OVER THERE
IN THE WALKING AREA.

681
00:33:01,247 --> 00:33:04,050
[CHUCKLING]

682
00:33:04,083 --> 00:33:07,053
YEAH, I'LL TAKE A WALK.

683
00:33:07,087 --> 00:33:09,588
- OVER TO KIRK DOUGLAS' HOUSE!
- [LAUGHTER]

684
00:33:12,325 --> 00:33:14,227
I'M SORRY ABOUT THAT.

685
00:33:14,260 --> 00:33:16,162
HE'S A COLLEAGUE OF MINE,
YOU KNOW?

686
00:33:16,195 --> 00:33:19,165
I GUESS TONIGHT HE JUST HAD
TOO MUCH TO DRINK.

687
00:33:19,198 --> 00:33:22,235
DON'T APOLOGIZE FOR HIM.
I MEAN, THE MAN'S GOT NO CLASS.

688
00:33:22,268 --> 00:33:25,738
HEY, HEY, HEY,
DON'T BLOW ON ME.

689
00:33:25,772 --> 00:33:27,873
I GUESS YOU'RE RIGHT.

690
00:33:27,907 --> 00:33:29,108
HE'S GOT NO CLASS.

691
00:33:29,175 --> 00:33:31,777
THE CHEESEBALL'S
GOT NO FREAKIN' CLASS.

692
00:33:31,810 --> 00:33:33,813
I'M UH, PAUL NILES.

693
00:33:33,847 --> 00:33:35,382
NATALIE BURKE.
NICE MEETING YOU.

694
00:33:35,415 --> 00:33:37,883
NICE TO SOON
BE SLEEPING WITH YOU.

695
00:33:41,153 --> 00:33:42,755
AND THIS DINOSAUR WAS FOUND

696
00:33:42,788 --> 00:33:45,190
WITH A HEAD STICKING OUT
OF ITS BUTT.

697
00:33:45,223 --> 00:33:48,795
IT'S THE ACTUAL SKELETON
OF A PUSHMI-PULLYU.

698
00:33:50,930 --> 00:33:51,930
YOU KNOW, HE WAS RIGHT.

699
00:33:51,963 --> 00:33:54,567
THE WALK IS MAKING ME
RETHINK MY LIFE.

700
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:56,168
I'M GOING TO SET UP
A CHARITABLE FUN

701
00:33:56,202 --> 00:34:00,205
TO HELP PEOPLE WHO PAW WOMEN.
YES, YES.

702
00:34:04,443 --> 00:34:06,978
SO THEY MIC TIRES AND FEET
IN THIS MOVIE,

703
00:34:07,012 --> 00:34:09,815
BUT NOT PEOPLE.

704
00:34:09,848 --> 00:34:13,252
- GOOD EVENING, GENTLEMEN.
- DON'T LET ME
INTERRUPT YOUR PORN.

705
00:34:14,987 --> 00:34:16,388
- EVENING.
- EVENING.

706
00:34:16,422 --> 00:34:18,792
EVENING MISTER YURI.
WHAT CAN I DO FOR YOU?

707
00:34:18,825 --> 00:34:21,127
I FORGOT MY KEYS.

708
00:34:21,160 --> 00:34:23,695
DO YOU MIND
OPENING THE LAB FOR ME?

709
00:34:23,763 --> 00:34:27,633
DON'T OPEN YOUR PANTS!
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

710
00:34:27,667 --> 00:34:29,002
SIR.

711
00:34:29,035 --> 00:34:31,170
THANK YOU.

712
00:34:31,203 --> 00:34:33,305
♪ TONIGHT'S THE NIGHT ♪

713
00:34:33,338 --> 00:34:35,642
♪ GONNA BE ALL RIGHT ♪

714
00:34:35,675 --> 00:34:38,912
ISN'T THAT
DOUGLAS WILDER THERE?

715
00:34:38,945 --> 00:34:42,013
MAN, I'M REALLY FALLING BEHIND
ON MY PENTHOUSES, HERE.

716
00:34:43,682 --> 00:34:44,850
OOH, PEOPLE REALLY LOVE

717
00:34:44,883 --> 00:34:47,553
THE WHOLE
ROASTED-WEREWOLF BUFFET.

718
00:34:49,755 --> 00:34:51,390
COME ON IN WITH ME.

719
00:34:51,423 --> 00:34:52,392
IT WON'T BE AS MUCH FUN,

720
00:34:52,425 --> 00:34:56,128
BUT HE KNOWS
HE CAN PAW THIS GUY.

721
00:34:56,162 --> 00:34:59,132
SO YOU COULDN'T BE
A REAL COP, HUH?

722
00:35:00,365 --> 00:35:01,467
YOU KNOW WHAT THAT IS?

723
00:35:01,500 --> 00:35:02,702
THAT'S THE LAST
SECURITY GUARD

724
00:35:02,735 --> 00:35:05,303
WHO DIDN'T WASH MY CAR
EVERY DAY.

725
00:35:07,907 --> 00:35:10,442
- NO?
- SKELETON OF CARLY SIMON,
MAYBE.

726
00:35:10,477 --> 00:35:13,913
THOSE ARE THE REMAINS
OF A WEREWOLF.

727
00:35:13,947 --> 00:35:17,015
JEEZ, WHAT DO THEY WRAP THESE
IN TITANIUM? COME ON!

728
00:35:17,048 --> 00:35:18,317
[HONK]

729
00:35:18,350 --> 00:35:21,187
- DID HE JUST HONK?
- INCREDIBLE.

730
00:35:24,457 --> 00:35:27,092
[YAWNS]

731
00:35:27,125 --> 00:35:29,328
NOW, THIS MAY CAUSE
UNDERWEAR STAINING.

732
00:35:29,362 --> 00:35:30,697
[GUARD]
WEREWOLF?

733
00:35:30,730 --> 00:35:33,265
[YURI]
THAT'S RIGHT.

734
00:35:33,298 --> 00:35:36,135
AND I'M ABOUT THE CREATE...

735
00:35:36,168 --> 00:35:38,070
A MODERN, MAN-MADE WEREWOLF.

736
00:35:38,103 --> 00:35:40,840
WHO NEEDS CORRECTIVE SHOES.
LOOK AT HIM.

737
00:35:44,943 --> 00:35:46,578
- WEREWOLF.
- [HONK]

738
00:35:46,612 --> 00:35:49,782
- COME ON, HAVE A DRINK.
- NO, I'M SORRY. I'M ON DUTY.

739
00:35:49,815 --> 00:35:51,517
COME ON.
TONIGHT'S A SPECIAL NIGHT.

740
00:35:51,550 --> 00:35:53,652
COME ON, HAVE A DRINK.
HERE.

741
00:35:53,685 --> 00:35:56,388
WELL, SINCE IT'S THE END
OF MY SHIFT

742
00:35:56,422 --> 00:35:58,723
- I'LL MAKE AN EXCEPTION.
- THAT'S MY MAN.

743
00:35:58,757 --> 00:36:01,027
I THINK THIS GUY
MAKES A LOT OF EXCEPTIONS.

744
00:36:01,060 --> 00:36:02,528
YEAH.

745
00:36:02,562 --> 00:36:05,765
SO... CHEERS.

746
00:36:05,798 --> 00:36:09,368
LET'S DRINK
TO OUR NEW FRIENDSHIP

747
00:36:09,402 --> 00:36:11,603
AND OUR FRIEND...

748
00:36:11,670 --> 00:36:12,938
THE WEREWOLF.

749
00:36:12,972 --> 00:36:14,373
I'LL DRINK TO THAT.

750
00:36:14,407 --> 00:36:17,377
BUT I'LL DRINK TO LINT THOUGH,
SO IT'S NOTHING SPECIAL.

751
00:36:21,580 --> 00:36:25,217
[GIGGLING]
IT TICKLES MY NOSE!

752
00:36:25,250 --> 00:36:27,185
I'M GOING TO GET
ALL SEXY NOW.

753
00:36:27,220 --> 00:36:29,388
YEAH, CHAMPAGNE!

754
00:36:29,422 --> 00:36:31,457
♪♪

755
00:36:36,662 --> 00:36:39,198
SO YOU REALLY
BELIEVE IN THIS STUFF, HUH?

756
00:36:39,232 --> 00:36:41,300
OH, YEAH.

757
00:36:41,333 --> 00:36:44,003
MY MOTHER USED TO TELL ME
FAIRYTALES ABOUT THIS.

758
00:36:44,037 --> 00:36:45,772
SHE WAS
A GREAT SECURITY GUARD.

759
00:36:45,805 --> 00:36:47,740
NEVER BELIEVED IT.

760
00:36:47,773 --> 00:36:50,375
- I'M FROM VENICE, ITALY.
- OH.

761
00:36:50,408 --> 00:36:52,612
SO YOU'RE CONNECTED.

762
00:36:52,645 --> 00:36:54,913
MY MOTHER'S PASSED AWAY.
GOD BLESS HER SOUL.

763
00:36:54,947 --> 00:36:56,315
YOU KNOW, I'VE NEVER REALLY
TALKED TO ANYONE

764
00:36:56,348 --> 00:36:58,583
BUT MY BUS DRIVER.
[SNIFFS]

765
00:36:58,617 --> 00:37:01,853
PEOPLE GENERALLY
DON'T LIKE ME.

766
00:37:01,887 --> 00:37:06,558
HELP, I'VE GOT LOCKJAW!

767
00:37:06,592 --> 00:37:07,893
WELL...

768
00:37:07,927 --> 00:37:11,363
I ADMIT MY MOM'S NOT DEAD.
I WAS JUST FLIRTING.

769
00:37:11,397 --> 00:37:14,167
I'M VERY...

770
00:37:14,200 --> 00:37:16,568
BETTER GET GOING.

771
00:37:19,005 --> 00:37:21,107
THANKS FOR EVERYTHING.

772
00:37:21,140 --> 00:37:23,375
COME ON, SWEEP THAT SKELETON
OFF THE TABLE,

773
00:37:23,408 --> 00:37:25,778
AND GIVE IN TO THE PASSION!

774
00:37:28,413 --> 00:37:31,883
- SEE YOU.
- I LEFT SOME ARTHUR TREACHER'S
BACK AT THE DESK.

775
00:37:33,285 --> 00:37:35,487
GEE, A PIG-DRUNK, PASSED OUT
SECURITY GUARD.

776
00:37:35,520 --> 00:37:37,957
WHO'S SURPRISED?

777
00:37:37,990 --> 00:37:42,260
AH, ROOM TEMPERATURE TOTT'S.

778
00:37:42,295 --> 00:37:45,063
WELL, THIS GUY'S ON HIS FOURTH
HAIRDO SINCE THE MOVIE STARTED.

779
00:37:45,097 --> 00:37:47,667
- [LAUGHS]
- YEAH.

780
00:37:49,835 --> 00:37:53,372
UGH, THIS IS MY LAST
SECURITY GUARD, I SWEAR.

781
00:37:57,410 --> 00:37:59,012
REJECTED FOR
THE SUPREME COURT,

782
00:37:59,045 --> 00:38:02,180
ROBERT BORK STRUGGLES
TO MAKE ENDS MEET.

783
00:38:06,318 --> 00:38:09,255
PBR ME, ASA DIE.

784
00:38:09,288 --> 00:38:12,892
FROM THE LAND
OF SKY-BLUE MURDER.

785
00:38:16,762 --> 00:38:18,130
WELL, I HATED
TO KNOCK HIM OUT,

786
00:38:18,163 --> 00:38:21,100
BUT HE WAS DUE
FOR HIS TETANUS BOOSTER.

787
00:38:27,172 --> 00:38:29,275
SO WE'RE GOING TO GET
A WEREWOLF THAT SITS AT A DESK

788
00:38:29,308 --> 00:38:31,143
AND ASKS PEOPLE TO SIGN IN.

789
00:38:31,177 --> 00:38:33,345
YEAH.

790
00:38:36,382 --> 00:38:40,052
I WISH MY FACE
COULD BE TIGHTER!

791
00:38:40,085 --> 00:38:43,055
SO YOU'RE AN ARCHAEOLOGIST.
THAT'S INCREDIBLE.

792
00:38:43,088 --> 00:38:45,623
WELL, I GRADUATED THIS YEAR...
[DIALOGUE CUTS OUT]

793
00:38:45,657 --> 00:38:47,292
HEY, COULD WE TURN DOWN
THE PERCY FAITH?

794
00:38:47,325 --> 00:38:49,495
NO...

795
00:38:49,528 --> 00:38:51,263
- YOU KNOW--
- YOUR ONES ARE GREAT.

796
00:38:51,330 --> 00:38:52,965
I REALLY ADMIRE YOU.

797
00:38:52,998 --> 00:38:56,868
- YOU DO?
- YEAH, SURE, WHATEVER.
CAN WE SLEEP TOGETHER?

798
00:38:56,902 --> 00:38:59,505
WELL, THANKS.

799
00:38:59,538 --> 00:39:02,475
SO TELL ME,
HAVE YOU MADE ANY, UH,

800
00:39:02,508 --> 00:39:04,543
HISTORY SHATTERING
DISCOVERIES LATELY?

801
00:39:04,577 --> 00:39:07,245
I BARELY KNOW WHAT A HAT IS.

802
00:39:07,278 --> 00:39:09,182
ENOUGH ABOUT ME.

803
00:39:09,215 --> 00:39:10,983
WHAT ABOUT YOU?
WHAT DO YOU DO?

804
00:39:11,017 --> 00:39:12,685
I LOOK DOWN YOUR DRESS
FOR A LIVING.

805
00:39:12,718 --> 00:39:15,253
- I'M A WRITER.
- OF THE PURPLE SAGE.

806
00:39:15,287 --> 00:39:17,322
AND I'M ACTUALLY
WORKING ON SOMETHING NOW.

807
00:39:17,355 --> 00:39:19,425
REALLY?
WHAT'S THE SUBJECT MATTER?

808
00:39:19,458 --> 00:39:22,227
YOU'RE RIGHT,
SUBJECT DOESN'T MATTER AT ALL.

809
00:39:22,260 --> 00:39:24,863
[LAUGHTER]
THAT'S A GOOD ONE.

810
00:39:24,897 --> 00:39:26,365
I LOVE THIS MUSIC.

811
00:39:26,398 --> 00:39:27,600
LET'S DANCE.

812
00:39:27,633 --> 00:39:29,968
YEAH, RICHARD CLAYDERMAN,
I LOVE HIM.

813
00:39:30,002 --> 00:39:32,938
MY MODERN MAN-MADE WEREWOLF.

814
00:39:32,972 --> 00:39:35,842
THE VERY MODEL
OF A MODERN MAN-MADE WEREWOLF.

815
00:39:39,112 --> 00:39:41,747
- HONEY.
- WAKE UP.

816
00:39:41,780 --> 00:39:44,283
- WHAT HAPPENED?
- YOU PASSED OUT.

817
00:39:44,317 --> 00:39:47,352
I OPENED UP MY GYM BAG
AND DOWN YOU WENT.

818
00:39:47,385 --> 00:39:49,422
- SORRY.
- COME ON.

819
00:39:49,455 --> 00:39:51,223
I KNOW.

820
00:39:51,257 --> 00:39:54,227
COME ON, GET UP.

821
00:39:56,595 --> 00:39:59,765
- YOU OKAY?
- YEAH, WELL, MY UNDERPANTS
ARE ON BACKWARDS.

822
00:39:59,798 --> 00:40:01,533
YEAH.

823
00:40:01,567 --> 00:40:04,503
YES.

824
00:40:04,537 --> 00:40:05,537
TAKE CARE.

825
00:40:05,570 --> 00:40:08,640
SEND IN
THE NEXT SECURITY GUARD.

826
00:40:08,673 --> 00:40:12,645
WELL, HE'S NO
RICHARD JEWELL, BUT.

827
00:40:14,280 --> 00:40:18,050
[WOLF HOWLING]

828
00:40:19,452 --> 00:40:21,020
HEY, IT'S NEIL YOUNG.

829
00:40:21,053 --> 00:40:23,188
I'VE BEEN-- UGH, MINER

830
00:40:23,222 --> 00:40:25,423
FOR-- UGH, HEART OF-- AH.

831
00:40:27,392 --> 00:40:30,528
GOLD.

832
00:40:30,562 --> 00:40:35,467
OH, MAN, FOUR RUNS
TO THE BORDER IN ONE NIGHT.

833
00:40:35,500 --> 00:40:39,070
HEY, MERLE HAGGARD'S
LOOKING PRETTY GOOD THESE DAYS.

834
00:40:41,573 --> 00:40:45,477
THE FULL MOON
DOGGEDLY REFUSES TO WANE.

835
00:40:48,780 --> 00:40:52,317
♪ HEY, ZIP-A-DEE DOO-DAH,
ZIP-A-DEE-AY ♪

836
00:40:54,387 --> 00:40:56,455
UGH.

837
00:40:56,488 --> 00:40:58,290
MAN, IT'S BEEN A HARD DAY.

838
00:40:58,323 --> 00:41:02,293
TIME FOR A FRISCO BURGER
IN FRONT OF THE X-FILES.

839
00:41:02,327 --> 00:41:04,397
MAN, I'VE GOT SO MANY
THREATENING LETTERS

840
00:41:04,430 --> 00:41:06,432
TO WRITE TONIGHT.

841
00:41:06,465 --> 00:41:09,435
- [MUSICAL STING]
- DID HE SIT ON A TABLE SAW?
WHAT IS THAT?

842
00:41:09,468 --> 00:41:11,003
[IMITATES TABLE SAW]

843
00:41:11,037 --> 00:41:13,438
OH, NOW THIS CLOWN'S GOT
BRYAN FERRY HAIR!

844
00:41:13,472 --> 00:41:16,008
WHAT'S GOING ON?

845
00:41:16,042 --> 00:41:18,710
[CHUCKLES]
♪ HELLO, DOLLY ♪

846
00:41:18,743 --> 00:41:21,647
♪ IT'S LOUIS, DOLLY ♪

847
00:41:27,385 --> 00:41:31,623
THE MOST STUBBORN FULL MOON
IN THE HISTORY OF THE WORLD.

848
00:41:31,690 --> 00:41:33,258
[CAR STARTS]

849
00:41:33,325 --> 00:41:36,262
OH, GREAT, KING TIMAHOE HERE'S
GONNA DRIVE HIMSELF HOME.

850
00:41:38,430 --> 00:41:41,900
I HOPE HE REMEMBERS
TO CRACK A WINDOW FOR HIMSELF.

851
00:41:52,612 --> 00:41:54,680
WEREWOLF'S HANGING HIS OWN HEAD
OUT OF THE WINDOW,

852
00:41:54,713 --> 00:41:57,282
RUNNING ALL OVER HIS OWN CAR.

853
00:42:00,552 --> 00:42:03,155
I'M COLORBLIND NOW.
WHAT DO I DO?

854
00:42:09,595 --> 00:42:11,063
LOOK AT THOSE
HIGH GAS PRICES.

855
00:42:11,097 --> 00:42:15,233
WHAT, ARE THEY
IN PORT-AU-PRINCE?

856
00:42:15,267 --> 00:42:18,337
YEAH. GOOD DOG.

857
00:42:18,370 --> 00:42:20,205
I WAS GONNA GO HOME
AND WATCH TV,

858
00:42:20,238 --> 00:42:23,775
BUT I FEEL LIKE SNIFFIN' BUTTS
ALL NIGHT.

859
00:42:23,808 --> 00:42:26,678
AH, MAN THIS TRAFFIC!

860
00:42:31,583 --> 00:42:33,352
WHAT, IS HE STALKING IT
BECAUSE IT'S THE WEAKEST

861
00:42:33,385 --> 00:42:36,088
OF ALL GAS STATIONS?

862
00:42:36,122 --> 00:42:38,457
♪ OH THE MIGHTY
BRONTOSAURUS ♪

863
00:42:38,490 --> 00:42:41,727
♪ DON'T YOU HAVE
A MESSAGE FOR US? ♪

864
00:42:45,430 --> 00:42:49,868
WHERE YOU LIVE IS INCREDIBLE.

865
00:42:49,902 --> 00:42:52,705
- SO HERE WE ARE.
- MR. SMOOTH.

866
00:42:52,738 --> 00:42:54,005
WOULD YOU LIKE TO COME UP
FOR A DRINK?

867
00:42:54,038 --> 00:42:55,942
OH, YEAH. THE ONE-TWO PUNCH.

868
00:42:55,975 --> 00:42:59,312
I GUESS I'D BETTER GO.
I HAVE A LOT TO DO TOMORROW.

869
00:42:59,345 --> 00:43:02,347
YEAH, IN OTHER WORDS,
YOU HATE ME! FINE!

870
00:43:05,952 --> 00:43:10,022
- PAUL?
- I ENJOYED YOUR LETTER
TO THE PHILIPPIANS.

871
00:43:13,292 --> 00:43:17,228
I LIKE SAYING NO TO YOU.
COULD YOU ASK ME AGAIN?

872
00:43:17,262 --> 00:43:19,565
WELCOME TO FLAGSTAFF.

873
00:43:19,632 --> 00:43:20,732
WELL, THANKS.

874
00:43:20,732 --> 00:43:23,435
WELCOME TO MY FLAGSTAFF,
IF YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN.

875
00:43:23,468 --> 00:43:25,903
- NO.
- SORRY.

876
00:43:30,742 --> 00:43:32,210
WHAT DO YOU GOT THERE, PAUL?

877
00:43:32,243 --> 00:43:34,078
HE'S TRAPPED
BETWEEN FIRST AND SECOND.

878
00:43:34,112 --> 00:43:36,848
- CAUGHT IN A RUN DOWN.
- SAM.

879
00:43:36,882 --> 00:43:41,453
SAM, THIS IS NATALIE.
NATALIE, THIS IS SAM THE KEEPER.

880
00:43:42,688 --> 00:43:44,222
NICE MEETING YOU, SAM.

881
00:43:44,255 --> 00:43:46,392
HOW DO YOU DO?

882
00:43:46,425 --> 00:43:49,060
WE CAN ALWAYS USE
ANOTHER PRETTY FACE AROUND HERE.

883
00:43:49,093 --> 00:43:53,232
- ANOTHER?
- ANY FRIEND OF PAUL'S
IS A FRIEND OF MINE.

884
00:43:53,265 --> 00:43:55,033
HE'S WONDERFUL.

885
00:43:55,067 --> 00:43:56,568
WELL, I GUESS
I'LL SEE YOU TOMORROW.

886
00:43:56,602 --> 00:43:57,870
YEAH. BYE.

887
00:43:57,903 --> 00:44:00,838
BRING THE OLD GUY, WILL YOU?

888
00:44:04,910 --> 00:44:06,212
- [GROWLING]
- [LAUGHTER]

889
00:44:06,245 --> 00:44:09,313
FEEL LIKE GETTING OUT
AND CHASING MY OWN TIRE.

890
00:44:13,885 --> 00:44:16,722
AN AMERICAN WEREWOLF
IN TRAFFIC.

891
00:44:18,023 --> 00:44:20,992
GREAT, WHAT ARE THE RAMP LIGHTS
STILL DOING ON?

892
00:44:22,160 --> 00:44:24,430
SAME GAS STATION.

893
00:44:26,532 --> 00:44:30,902
I'M GONNA FOLLOW
THE HELL OUT OF HIM.

894
00:44:30,935 --> 00:44:32,037
NOW THAT I'M DRIVING,

895
00:44:32,070 --> 00:44:35,140
THOSE CARIBOU
DON'T STAND A CHANCE.

896
00:44:39,110 --> 00:44:40,412
OH!

897
00:44:40,445 --> 00:44:44,917
DID THOSE OIL BARRELS
JUST LEAP OUT IN FRONT OF HIM?

898
00:44:44,950 --> 00:44:47,152
SO HIS PLAN IS TO RID THE WORLD
OF SECURITY GUARDS

899
00:44:47,185 --> 00:44:49,153
BY CHANGING THEM INTO WEREWOLVES
ONE BY ONE,

900
00:44:49,187 --> 00:44:50,922
AND THEN HAVING THEM
CRASH THEIR CARS.

901
00:44:50,955 --> 00:44:53,558
WELL, UH, SEEMS TO BE
WORKING SO FAR.

902
00:44:53,592 --> 00:44:55,760
- CAN'T FAULT HIM ON THAT.
- NO.

903
00:44:55,793 --> 00:44:56,862
HUH.

904
00:44:56,895 --> 00:44:58,463
♪♪

905
00:45:04,202 --> 00:45:06,003
HEY, SUSIE,
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

906
00:45:06,037 --> 00:45:07,538
YEAH, SUSIE, WHAT'S WRONG?

907
00:45:07,572 --> 00:45:09,408
AH, NOTHING I GUESS.

908
00:45:09,475 --> 00:45:10,942
COME ON, SUSIE,
YOU CAN TELL US.

909
00:45:10,975 --> 00:45:12,510
- YEAH.
- GEE, I DON'T KNOW, GIRLS.

910
00:45:12,543 --> 00:45:14,847
- WELL, OKAY, IT'S LIKE THIS.
- UH-HUH?

911
00:45:14,880 --> 00:45:17,950
- YOU KNOW STEVE?
- UH-HUH!

912
00:45:17,983 --> 00:45:20,885
♪ STEVE'S A WEREWOLF,
BUT HE'S MY GUY ♪

913
00:45:20,918 --> 00:45:23,522
♪ HE'S DIFFERENT FROM THE REST
I DON'T KNOW WHY ♪

914
00:45:23,555 --> 00:45:26,958
♪ BUT MY MOTHER AND POP,
THEY DISAPPROVE ♪

915
00:45:26,992 --> 00:45:29,895
♪ BUT NO ONE CAN STOP US,
FOR IT'S TRUE "LOUVE" ♪

916
00:45:29,928 --> 00:45:31,297
- HUH?
- "LOUVE?"

917
00:45:31,330 --> 00:45:32,530
WELL, I HAD TO RHYME TWO WORDS.
THEY'RE NOT THE SAME--

918
00:45:32,563 --> 00:45:33,965
- SURE. GO ON.
- GOT IT, GOT IT, GO AHEAD.

919
00:45:33,998 --> 00:45:36,635
♪ WHERE, OH, WEREWOLF ♪
♪ SHOO-BI-DOOWOP-DOOWOP ♪

920
00:45:36,668 --> 00:45:40,138
♪ I'VE LOOKED EVERY WEREWOLF ♪
♪ SHOO-BI-DOOWOP-DOOWOP ♪

921
00:45:40,172 --> 00:45:42,975
♪ WHERE, OH, WHERE ♪
♪ SHOO-BI-DOOWOP-DOOWOP ♪

922
00:45:43,008 --> 00:45:47,012
♪ WHERE IS MY WEREWOLF? ♪
♪ SHOO-BI-DOOWOP-DOOWOP ♪

923
00:45:47,045 --> 00:45:50,848
LISTEN UP, GIRLS.
♪ LATE ONE NIGHT,
WE DROVE IN HIS CAR ♪

924
00:45:50,882 --> 00:45:53,452
♪ TO MAKE OUT POINT,
IT WASN'T THAT FAR ♪

925
00:45:53,485 --> 00:45:55,853
TAKE THE HIAWATHA EXIT.
LEFT AT THE FIRST STOP SIGN.

926
00:45:55,887 --> 00:45:57,222
UH, WHOSE STORY
IS THIS, CAROL?

927
00:45:57,255 --> 00:45:58,923
SORRY!
[CHUCKLES]

928
00:45:58,957 --> 00:46:02,027
♪ THE MOON WAS FULL,
HE PULLED ME CLOSE ♪

929
00:46:02,060 --> 00:46:04,730
♪ I HELD HIS PAW
AND I TOUCHED HIS COLD NOSE ♪

930
00:46:04,763 --> 00:46:06,898
THAT MEANS HE'S HEALTHY!

931
00:46:06,932 --> 00:46:09,502
♪ BUT JUST THEN HIS HAIRY PAWS
CAUSED THE WHEEL TO SLIDE ♪

932
00:46:09,535 --> 00:46:11,703
- [GASPS]
- I SCREAMED, TOO LATE,
WE HIT A TREE!

933
00:46:11,737 --> 00:46:15,140
- HE DIED.
- GEE, THAT'S TOO BAD, SUSIE.

934
00:46:15,173 --> 00:46:17,843
♪ WHERE, OH, WEREWOLF ♪

935
00:46:17,877 --> 00:46:21,112
♪ I'VE LOOKED
EVERYWHERE-WOLF ♪

936
00:46:21,147 --> 00:46:24,048
♪ WHERE, OH, WHERE ♪

937
00:46:24,082 --> 00:46:26,452
♪ WHERE, OH, WHERE,
OH, WHERE ♪

938
00:46:26,485 --> 00:46:29,822
♪ IS MY WEREWOLF? ♪

939
00:46:29,855 --> 00:46:32,290
♪ WEREWOLF ♪

940
00:46:32,323 --> 00:46:33,658
[LAUGHTER]

941
00:46:33,692 --> 00:46:35,093
WELL DONE.

942
00:46:35,127 --> 00:46:36,262
YEAH, IT'S FUN
TO PLAY A GIRL GROUP,

943
00:46:36,295 --> 00:46:37,462
EVEN IF IT'S JUST FOR A WHILE.

944
00:46:37,495 --> 00:46:41,833
- YEAH, JUST A WHILE.
- YEAH, THAT WAS FUN.

945
00:46:41,867 --> 00:46:44,603
WELL, HEY, SAY, MIKE
YOU DIDN'T REALLY GO OUT

946
00:46:44,637 --> 00:46:47,338
WITH A GUY NAMED STEVE
WHO DIED, DID YOU? OR...

947
00:46:47,372 --> 00:46:48,740
WELL, YOU KNOW,
THERE IS A STORY--

948
00:46:48,773 --> 00:46:49,875
[BUZZER SOUNDS]

949
00:46:49,908 --> 00:46:50,875
- MOVIES!
- OH, LATER. WE GOT MOVIE SIGN!

950
00:46:50,908 --> 00:46:53,378
SAVE IT FOR LATER.

951
00:47:03,955 --> 00:47:06,090
- UGH, THAT WAS FUN.
- YEAH.

952
00:47:06,123 --> 00:47:07,392
SO, PAUL, WHAT DO YOU THINK?

953
00:47:07,425 --> 00:47:09,127
COULD THE COLOSSIANS
STAND ANOTHER LETTER?

954
00:47:09,160 --> 00:47:12,497
WELL, UH, I'M IMPRESSED.
I NEVER SEEN ANYTHING LIKE THIS.

955
00:47:12,530 --> 00:47:13,965
A GIRL WHO RESPONDS TO ME.

956
00:47:13,998 --> 00:47:17,302
BUT JUST OUT OF CURIOSITY,
WHAT MAKES YOU SO CERTAIN

957
00:47:17,335 --> 00:47:19,538
THAT THIS THING
IS A WEREWOLF?

958
00:47:19,572 --> 00:47:22,240
I MEAN, I DON'T WANT
TO SOUND SKEPTICAL,

959
00:47:22,273 --> 00:47:24,108
- BUT--
- BUT THIS IS SUCH CRAP.

960
00:47:24,142 --> 00:47:25,777
COULDN'T IT BE SOME KIND
OF A DEFORMED ANIMAL?

961
00:47:25,810 --> 00:47:29,213
LIKE A BEAR OR A COYOTE
OR SOMETHING?

962
00:47:29,247 --> 00:47:30,382
CHICKEN, CAPUBERA.

963
00:47:30,415 --> 00:47:33,385
WHY A WEREWOLF?
I DON'T UNDERSTAND THAT.

964
00:47:33,418 --> 00:47:36,788
WELL, LOOK, WHEN NOEL GETS HERE
HE CAN EXPLAIN IT IN DETAIL.

965
00:47:36,822 --> 00:47:39,592
BUT LET ME
SHOW YOU SOMETHING.

966
00:47:39,625 --> 00:47:42,027
WHEN YOU LOOK
AT THE STRUCTURE OF THE LEG,

967
00:47:42,060 --> 00:47:45,297
- YOU CAN SEE--
- THAT I AM STALLING.

968
00:47:45,330 --> 00:47:47,198
OH, THAT MUST BE NOEL NOW.
[CHUCKLES]

969
00:47:47,198 --> 00:47:50,802
- OH, YURI.
- BOOM, ANOTHER HAIRSTYLE.

970
00:47:50,835 --> 00:47:52,603
WHAT'S HE DOING HERE?

971
00:47:52,637 --> 00:47:54,438
DON'T YOU KNOW
THIS IS RESTRICTED AREA?

972
00:47:54,472 --> 00:47:56,408
YURI, PAUL'S BEEN CLEARED
BY NOEL.

973
00:47:56,442 --> 00:47:59,410
HE'S HERE TO HELP US
GET MORE RESEARCH FUNDING.

974
00:47:59,443 --> 00:48:02,047
RELAX, THERE'S NO CALL
FOR UNPLEASANTNESS HERE.

975
00:48:02,080 --> 00:48:03,415
WHERE DID YOU GET
THIS CLOWN?

976
00:48:03,448 --> 00:48:05,517
HEY, LOOK,
I REALLY DON'T NEED THIS.

977
00:48:05,550 --> 00:48:06,518
I DIDN'T COME DOWN HERE

978
00:48:06,552 --> 00:48:08,020
TO BE INSULTED
BY A PSYCHOPATH.

979
00:48:08,053 --> 00:48:09,655
YOU CALLING ME A PSYCHOPATH?

980
00:48:09,688 --> 00:48:11,657
I'LL KILL YOUR WHOLE FAMILY
IF YOU CALL ME THAT AGAIN!

981
00:48:11,690 --> 00:48:12,823
NO, STOP IT!

982
00:48:12,857 --> 00:48:14,525
ACTION PAUL!

983
00:48:14,558 --> 00:48:18,597
- OOH!
- YURI, STOP IT.

984
00:48:18,630 --> 00:48:20,565
OH, THE WIND FROM THE SKULL
IS KNOCKING ME OVER!

985
00:48:20,598 --> 00:48:22,267
STOP IT! STOP IT!

986
00:48:22,300 --> 00:48:24,168
GET OUT OF HERE!

987
00:48:24,202 --> 00:48:25,970
WHOA, THEY BETTER HAVE
ANOTHER ONE OF THESE JACKETS

988
00:48:26,003 --> 00:48:27,905
AT CHESS KING.

989
00:48:27,940 --> 00:48:30,242
GET OUT!

990
00:48:30,275 --> 00:48:32,610
GET OUT OF HERE!

991
00:48:32,643 --> 00:48:34,378
- GET OUT!
- I'M REALLY SORRY.

992
00:48:34,412 --> 00:48:37,748
CLEARLY YOU'RE NOT A PSYCHOPATH.
MY MISTAKE.

993
00:48:37,782 --> 00:48:40,152
GET OUT BEFORE MY DOG TELLS ME
TO SHOOT THE PRESIDENT.

994
00:48:40,152 --> 00:48:42,787
PAUL! PAUL!

995
00:48:42,820 --> 00:48:44,623
THIS IS LIKE THAT TIME
I HIT THAT REPORTER

996
00:48:44,657 --> 00:48:49,093
WITH PILTDOWN MAN'S
THIGHBONE.

997
00:48:49,127 --> 00:48:51,062
THE MOVIE'S BIGGEST FAN.

998
00:48:51,095 --> 00:48:53,632
- HOO-HOO!
- [CHUCKLES]

999
00:48:53,665 --> 00:48:54,833
SHE CAN'T HELP BUT BE IMPRESSED

1000
00:48:54,867 --> 00:48:56,568
BY THE WAY
I HANDLED THAT SITUATION.

1001
00:48:56,602 --> 00:48:59,838
THE WAY I SCURRIED OUT
WHEN HE ORDERED ME TO.

1002
00:49:04,175 --> 00:49:06,010
YOU KNOW, IF YOU LOOK AT IT
A CERTAIN WAY,

1003
00:49:06,043 --> 00:49:11,417
I ACTUALLY WON THAT FIGHT.

1004
00:49:11,450 --> 00:49:13,718
AH.

1005
00:49:13,752 --> 00:49:14,720
WELL, THEY CAST ME.

1006
00:49:14,753 --> 00:49:17,922
I GUESS THEY WANT ME
TO DO SOMETHING.

1007
00:49:17,955 --> 00:49:23,228
FLAGSTAFF. I CAN'T BELIEVE
I'M STILL IN FLAGSTAFF.

1008
00:49:23,262 --> 00:49:26,732
OH, WEASELS
RIPPED MY FLESH AGAIN.

1009
00:49:26,765 --> 00:49:30,368
WORD OF ADVICE,
NEVER HAVE SEX WITH FLO-JO.

1010
00:49:33,738 --> 00:49:35,740
♪ AAH ♪

1011
00:49:40,545 --> 00:49:42,080
[GRUNTING]

1012
00:49:42,113 --> 00:49:43,882
- STOP IT.
- STOP IT, IMMEDIATELY.

1013
00:49:43,915 --> 00:49:45,750
HEY!

1014
00:49:45,783 --> 00:49:50,688
IT'S THE RED SHOE DIARIES
ALL OF A SUDDEN.

1015
00:49:50,722 --> 00:49:53,625
ROH, RAT WAS RANRASTIC.

1016
00:49:56,562 --> 00:50:00,865
DAYLIGHT ON THE INSIDE,
NIGHT TIME OUTDOORS.

1017
00:50:00,898 --> 00:50:03,768
AND BACK TO WANING DAYLIGHT
OUTSIDE. OKAY.

1018
00:50:08,173 --> 00:50:12,043
♪ LA ♪

1019
00:50:12,077 --> 00:50:15,213
V--, ZIP, EE--...

1020
00:50:18,883 --> 00:50:21,018
I GOT MONO.

1021
00:50:21,052 --> 00:50:24,790
♪ LA ♪

1022
00:50:24,823 --> 00:50:26,323
♪♪ [MUSICAL STING]

1023
00:50:26,357 --> 00:50:29,093
THERE'S THAT TABLE SAW AGAIN.

1024
00:50:32,597 --> 00:50:34,933
HE'S DOING IYEN-GRR YOGA.

1025
00:50:34,967 --> 00:50:38,570
- HOO-HOO!
- GOOD ONE.

1026
00:50:38,603 --> 00:50:41,205
[GRUNTING]

1027
00:50:43,342 --> 00:50:44,977
[GROWLING]

1028
00:50:45,010 --> 00:50:46,712
OH, IF I COULD JUST FART.

1029
00:50:46,745 --> 00:50:49,680
AW.

1030
00:50:49,713 --> 00:50:51,282
YOU KNOW, THE ANTIDOTE
TO BEING A WEREWOLF

1031
00:50:51,315 --> 00:50:53,218
JUST MIGHT BE IMODIUM A-D.

1032
00:50:53,252 --> 00:50:54,920
I DON'T WANT TO BE NEAR HIM.

1033
00:50:54,953 --> 00:50:58,022
[PAINED MOANS]

1034
00:50:58,055 --> 00:51:01,192
- GONNA THROW UP.
- YUCK.

1035
00:51:01,225 --> 00:51:02,927
SO ARE WE SUPPOSED TO ASSUME
A MONTH PASSES

1036
00:51:02,960 --> 00:51:05,830
EVERY FEW MINUTES
HERE IN FLAGSTAFF?

1037
00:51:07,532 --> 00:51:09,700
♪♪ [VIOLIN CHORD]

1038
00:51:09,733 --> 00:51:13,272
ALL ABOARD.

1039
00:51:13,305 --> 00:51:16,642
THE DANGER OF HAIR OIL
GRAPHICALLY PORTRAYED.

1040
00:51:18,343 --> 00:51:21,045
♪ LA ♪

1041
00:51:22,680 --> 00:51:26,417
OH, WOULD HE JUST
TRANSFORM ALREADY? JEEZ!

1042
00:51:28,720 --> 00:51:32,457
♪ LA ♪

1043
00:51:32,490 --> 00:51:36,027
♪♪ [IMITATING NATIVE AMERICAN
TRIBAL MUSIC]

1044
00:51:38,797 --> 00:51:42,167
BACON, BACON, BACON!

1045
00:51:48,207 --> 00:51:51,308
READY, WRESTLE.

1046
00:51:53,978 --> 00:51:57,082
PHOTOGRAPHED
BY DANNY DeVITO.

1047
00:51:57,115 --> 00:51:58,717
NO, HE DOES THIS
ALL THE TIME.

1048
00:51:58,750 --> 00:52:01,520
IT HAS NOTHING TO DO
WITH BEING A WEREWOLF.

1049
00:52:01,553 --> 00:52:03,688
COEN BROTHERS' SCENE.

1050
00:52:03,722 --> 00:52:07,425
DIRECTOR GOT TO BORROW
HIS COUSIN'S DOLLY FOR A WEEK.

1051
00:52:10,195 --> 00:52:14,165
A TREE IN SPRING.

1052
00:52:14,198 --> 00:52:15,433
HELLO, PAUL?

1053
00:52:15,500 --> 00:52:18,803
I'M NOT LICHENTHROPISING!
[NERVOUS CHUCKLE]

1054
00:52:22,473 --> 00:52:26,678
UM, THE DEAD SHEEP WAS HERE
WHEN I MOVED IN.

1055
00:52:26,712 --> 00:52:29,848
I'M FIXING MYSELF A DRINK.
YOU WANT ONE?

1056
00:52:29,882 --> 00:52:33,718
UH, SURE. I'LL HAVE
WHATEVER YOU'RE HAVING. THANKS.

1057
00:52:33,752 --> 00:52:35,920
[CHUCKLES]

1058
00:52:35,953 --> 00:52:39,823
HEY, GREAT.
UH, TOILET WATER OKAY?

1059
00:52:39,858 --> 00:52:43,127
UH, HEY, YOUR GIRL-GROUP WIG
IS ON CROOKED.

1060
00:52:43,160 --> 00:52:45,263
I DIDN'T THINK I WOULD EVER
HEAR FROM YOU AGAIN.

1061
00:52:45,297 --> 00:52:47,232
I TRIED TO STOP YOU
WHEN YOU LEFT THE LAB,

1062
00:52:47,265 --> 00:52:49,400
BUT YOUR TAXI DROVE OFF
BEFORE I COULD CATCH YOU.

1063
00:52:49,433 --> 00:52:50,402
COME ON, YOU DON'T
HAVE TO WORRY.

1064
00:52:50,435 --> 00:52:51,402
I'LL PAY FOR ANY DAMAGES.

1065
00:52:51,435 --> 00:52:53,003
VOICE COACH
WAS DAVID DUCHOVNY.

1066
00:52:53,037 --> 00:52:55,040
COME ON, PAUL.
DON'T BE LIKE THAT.

1067
00:52:55,073 --> 00:52:58,210
WHY NOT? I SCREWED EVERYTHING UP
DIDN'T I?

1068
00:52:58,243 --> 00:52:59,410
"SCOOED"?

1069
00:52:59,443 --> 00:53:01,278
NO, PAUL, YOU DIDN'T.

1070
00:53:01,312 --> 00:53:03,815
WHAT HAPPENED AT THE LAB
WASN'T YOUR FAULT.

1071
00:53:03,848 --> 00:53:07,485
YOU WET YOUR PANTS AND RAN,
AND THAT'S FINE.

1072
00:53:09,387 --> 00:53:12,457
COME ON, NATALIE.
IT NEVER WOULD HAVE HAPPENED
IF I HADN'T BEEN THERE.

1073
00:53:12,490 --> 00:53:14,458
WHAT HAPPENED
WAS ONLY YURI'S FAULT.

1074
00:53:14,492 --> 00:53:16,795
I EXPLAINED EVERYTHING TO NOEL.
HE DOESN'T BLAME YOU.

1075
00:53:16,828 --> 00:53:18,230
HE KNOWS HOW YURI IS.

1076
00:53:18,263 --> 00:53:19,430
THAT DOESN'T REPAIR
THE DAMAGE,

1077
00:53:19,463 --> 00:53:20,798
I MEAN,
YOUR FIND WAS DISTURBED.

1078
00:53:20,832 --> 00:53:22,133
IT WASN'T AS BAD
AS IT LOOKED.

1079
00:53:22,167 --> 00:53:25,103
THERE WAS NO
IRREPARABLE DAMAGE.

1080
00:53:25,137 --> 00:53:29,507
THE BONES WEREN'T BAD.
WE CAN PIECE THEM BACK TOGETHER.

1081
00:53:29,540 --> 00:53:31,610
BELIEVE ME.
I DO THIS FOR A LIVING.

1082
00:53:31,643 --> 00:53:34,512
YOU CONSOLE EUROPEAN LOSERS?

1083
00:53:34,545 --> 00:53:37,015
- I HOPE YOU'RE RIGHT.
- OF COURSE I'M RIGHT.

1084
00:53:37,048 --> 00:53:39,417
- ARE YOU SURE?
- OF COURSE I'M SURE.

1085
00:53:39,450 --> 00:53:42,820
NOW, GET OFF YOUR GUILT TRIP.
WE STILL NEED YOUR HELP.

1086
00:53:42,853 --> 00:53:45,623
YOU MIGHT BE
JUST OUR LAST HOPE.

1087
00:53:45,657 --> 00:53:47,225
SO WHAT DO YOU SAY?

1088
00:53:47,258 --> 00:53:49,660
SOMEDAY I'M SURE THEY'LL EXPLAIN
WHAT HE'S THE LAST HOPE FOR.

1089
00:53:49,693 --> 00:53:50,728
I'D LOVE TO.

1090
00:53:50,762 --> 00:53:54,165
- THAT'S GREAT.
- [WINCES]

1091
00:53:54,198 --> 00:53:55,367
PAUL, WHAT'S WRONG?

1092
00:53:55,400 --> 00:53:56,968
NOTHING.
REALLY, IT'S NOTHING.

1093
00:53:57,002 --> 00:53:59,170
IT'S JUST A SCRATCH
FROM MY FIGHT WITH YURI.

1094
00:53:59,203 --> 00:54:02,407
- WELL, LET ME SEE.
- NO, NO, NO.
COME ON, IT'S NOTHING.

1095
00:54:02,440 --> 00:54:04,142
TAKE OFF YOUR SHIRT.

1096
00:54:04,175 --> 00:54:07,678
ALL RIGHT,
BUT I'M TELLING YOU, IT'S--

1097
00:54:07,712 --> 00:54:11,515
OH, IT REALLY IS NOTHING.
QUIT YOUR CRYING.

1098
00:54:11,548 --> 00:54:14,118
THIS IS NOT A SCRATCH,
IT'S A DEEP CUT.

1099
00:54:14,152 --> 00:54:15,420
UH, SPEAKING OF DEEP CUTS,

1100
00:54:15,453 --> 00:54:17,622
DOES THIS SCENE
NEED TO BE IN THE MOVIE?

1101
00:54:17,655 --> 00:54:21,960
♪ LOVE, SOFT AS
A WEREWOLF PELT ♪

1102
00:54:23,762 --> 00:54:26,230
YOU KNOW, IF SHE'S SCRATCHES
HIS BELLY, HIS LEG WILL SHAKE.

1103
00:54:26,263 --> 00:54:27,965
[CHUCKLES]

1104
00:54:27,998 --> 00:54:31,568
♪ ZIGGY PLAYED GUITAR ♪

1105
00:54:35,240 --> 00:54:38,943
[HOWLS]

1106
00:54:38,977 --> 00:54:42,280
- REGGIE MANTLE, NO!
- BUT VERONICA...

1107
00:54:43,782 --> 00:54:45,683
WELL, THAT'S OKAY.
IT HAPPENS TO EVERYONE.

1108
00:54:45,717 --> 00:54:48,653
WELL, IT HAPPENS TO YOU.
A LOT.

1109
00:54:48,687 --> 00:54:51,055
WHAT SEEMS TO BE
THE PROBLEM, FELLA?

1110
00:54:51,088 --> 00:54:53,290
[LAUGHS]
MY ZIPPER'S STUCK.

1111
00:54:53,325 --> 00:54:55,760
- UGH.
- [GIGGLING]

1112
00:54:55,760 --> 00:54:57,562
YOU KNOW WHAT,
WHY DON'T WE

1113
00:54:57,595 --> 00:54:59,730
START THE FESTIVITIES
IN THE BACK SEAT?

1114
00:54:59,763 --> 00:55:01,867
GOT SOME WD-40 BACK HERE.

1115
00:55:01,900 --> 00:55:04,235
DID YOU BRING THE RAINCOAT?

1116
00:55:04,268 --> 00:55:05,637
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

1117
00:55:05,670 --> 00:55:07,272
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN.

1118
00:55:07,305 --> 00:55:09,273
YOU KNOW, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT THE BIG DEAL IS.

1119
00:55:09,307 --> 00:55:10,875
- WE AREN'T EVEN NAKED YET.
- OH.

1120
00:55:10,908 --> 00:55:12,610
I JUST WANT TO KNOW
IF YOU BROUGHT ONE.

1121
00:55:12,643 --> 00:55:14,878
THAT'S IT. AH, TOO LATE.

1122
00:55:14,912 --> 00:55:17,015
- AH, FORGET IT.
- OH, SWEETIE.

1123
00:55:17,048 --> 00:55:18,617
- NO, NO, YOU BLEW IT.
- I DIDN'T MEAN--

1124
00:55:18,650 --> 00:55:20,485
- I DIDN'T MEAN TO UPSET YOU.
- YOU RUINED THE MOOD.

1125
00:55:20,518 --> 00:55:21,987
AND WHAT A MOOD IT WAS.

1126
00:55:22,020 --> 00:55:23,555
- SWEETIE...
- NO.

1127
00:55:23,588 --> 00:55:26,623
WHERE'S THE KEYS?

1128
00:55:26,657 --> 00:55:29,193
- WHERE'D YOU HIDE THOSE KEYS?
- [GIGGLES]

1129
00:55:29,227 --> 00:55:31,195
I BET I CAN FINE 'EM.

1130
00:55:31,228 --> 00:55:33,063
[LAUGHS]

1131
00:55:33,097 --> 00:55:36,067
I KNOW HOW HE FEELS.
I LOST MY KEYS ONCE TOO.

1132
00:55:36,100 --> 00:55:37,102
-YEAH.
-YUP.

1133
00:55:37,135 --> 00:55:39,303
- OH, MY GOD!
- IT'S MY DAD!

1134
00:55:39,337 --> 00:55:40,905
DON'T GO WITHOUT ME!

1135
00:55:40,938 --> 00:55:43,375
- OH! OH!
- WAIT! WAIT!

1136
00:55:43,408 --> 00:55:45,510
OH, DEAR.

1137
00:55:45,543 --> 00:55:47,978
SO WHATEVER THEY DID IN THE BED
BLEW HIM OUT OF HIS ROOM

1138
00:55:48,012 --> 00:55:49,713
AND HALFWAY ACROSS TOWN.

1139
00:55:49,747 --> 00:55:51,950
OH, MY GOD!
[SCREAMING]

1140
00:55:51,950 --> 00:55:54,685
BIG...[PANTING]... WEREWOLF.

1141
00:55:54,718 --> 00:55:56,453
IT'S EDDIE VEDDER!

1142
00:55:56,487 --> 00:55:59,557
AAH!

1143
00:55:59,590 --> 00:56:01,625
WHEN CONFRONTED BY A WEREWOLF,
THIS IS IMPORTANT,

1144
00:56:01,658 --> 00:56:05,063
IMMEDIATELY LEAVE YOUR CAR
AND RUN OUT IN THE OPEN, OKAY.

1145
00:56:05,097 --> 00:56:06,563
[SCREAMING]

1146
00:56:06,597 --> 00:56:07,832
[HOWLING]

1147
00:56:07,865 --> 00:56:09,667
HE'S A WEREWORM.

1148
00:56:09,700 --> 00:56:12,737
AND HE'S COMING AT HER
AT A FRIGHTENING PACE.

1149
00:56:12,770 --> 00:56:15,005
[SCREAMS]

1150
00:56:15,038 --> 00:56:16,540
SOMEBODY'S
HELPING HER SCREAM.

1151
00:56:16,573 --> 00:56:20,745
YOU HEAR THAT TOO?

1152
00:56:20,778 --> 00:56:23,915
SINEAD O'CONNOR
FLEES PRINCE'S HOUSE.

1153
00:56:23,948 --> 00:56:28,487
♪ [HUMS CHASE MUSIC]

1154
00:56:30,422 --> 00:56:32,390
WAIT, HER DRESS IS PRE-MUDDY.

1155
00:56:32,423 --> 00:56:34,192
SUDDENLY
SHE'S A MEDIEVAL WENCH.

1156
00:56:34,225 --> 00:56:35,793
[SCREAMING CONTINUES]

1157
00:56:35,827 --> 00:56:40,465
MUD... IMPOSSIBLE
TO GET THROUGH MUD.

1158
00:56:40,498 --> 00:56:42,300
I WAS PLAYING MISS HAVISHAM
IN THE SCHOOL PLAY

1159
00:56:42,367 --> 00:56:45,670
WHEN I WAS ATTACKED
BY A WEREWOLF!

1160
00:56:45,703 --> 00:56:48,507
♪ AND ONE, AND TWO,
AND STEP, CHANGE, AND SHUFFLE ♪

1161
00:56:48,540 --> 00:56:51,408
♪ AND SEVEN, AND EIGHT,
AND WEREWOLF ♪

1162
00:56:51,442 --> 00:56:52,910
AAH!

1163
00:56:52,943 --> 00:56:54,945
♪ YOU GET A LOT OF DIRT
WITH WEREWOLVES ♪

1164
00:56:54,978 --> 00:56:59,383
♪ YOU GET A LOT OF CLEAN
WITH TIDE ♪

1165
00:56:59,417 --> 00:57:02,853
CAN'T YOU SEE WHAT I'M TRYING
TO TELL YOU? I LOVE YOU.

1166
00:57:08,493 --> 00:57:11,495
[IMITATES GURGLING SOUND]

1167
00:57:14,232 --> 00:57:16,300
BUTTERFLY KISSES
GONE HORRIBLY WRONG.

1168
00:57:16,333 --> 00:57:19,537
BETTER-DIE KISSES!

1169
00:57:19,570 --> 00:57:23,575
HE'S GETTING SOME HEALTHY REVERB
OFF OF HIS HOWLING.

1170
00:57:25,008 --> 00:57:27,478
UM, UH, THANKS.

1171
00:57:27,512 --> 00:57:30,648
I'LL CALL YOU. BYE.

1172
00:57:33,317 --> 00:57:37,988
HEY, HONEY, I FINALLY
GOT THE ZIPPER DOWN.

1173
00:57:38,055 --> 00:57:39,923
[HOWLING]

1174
00:57:39,957 --> 00:57:43,728
THE THIRD STRAIGHT WEEK
OF THE FULL MOON.

1175
00:57:43,762 --> 00:57:46,130
HE'S READING, "SO YOU THINK
YOU'RE A WEREWOLF."

1176
00:57:46,163 --> 00:57:49,967
- BY TOM AND VIRGINIA.
- WOLF.

1177
00:57:50,000 --> 00:57:52,703
OH, JOHN GRISHAM'S PROSE
IS JUST BEAUTIFUL.

1178
00:57:52,737 --> 00:57:53,905
I'M OVERCOME.

1179
00:57:53,938 --> 00:57:56,573
[HOWLING]

1180
00:58:02,847 --> 00:58:05,483
YOU KNOW, JUST NOT MY IDEA
OF A WEREWOLF.

1181
00:58:05,517 --> 00:58:07,418
I MEAN, HE'S SOMEWHAT
HIRSUTE, BUT...

1182
00:58:07,452 --> 00:58:08,953
YOU KNOW, IT TURNS OUT
HE'S NOT A WEREWOLF,

1183
00:58:08,987 --> 00:58:11,788
- HE'S JUST GREEK.
- AH.

1184
00:58:11,822 --> 00:58:15,393
I WAS FRAMED, I TELL YOU,
FRAMED!

1185
00:58:15,427 --> 00:58:19,097
OH, MAN, IF ONLY
I HAD SOME PAMPRIN.

1186
00:58:19,130 --> 00:58:22,267
[WOLF HOWLS]

1187
00:58:22,300 --> 00:58:24,035
WELL, THAT'S A...

1188
00:58:24,068 --> 00:58:26,237
BILL WALTON! NO, TOM WAITS.

1189
00:58:26,270 --> 00:58:27,838
NO, THE LEAD SINGER
FROM THE SPIN DOCTORS.

1190
00:58:27,872 --> 00:58:29,573
NO, IT'S ZACHARY TAYLOR!
THAT'S IT.

1191
00:58:29,607 --> 00:58:31,742
THAT'S IT.

1192
00:58:31,808 --> 00:58:33,978
- [QUACKING SOUNDS]
- SOME DUCK IN THE ROOM?

1193
00:58:34,012 --> 00:58:37,348
QUACK, QUACK, QUACK.

1194
00:58:37,382 --> 00:58:41,018
HE'S BECOMING
WERE-DANIEL STERN.

1195
00:58:44,388 --> 00:58:46,690
OH, I BIT MY LIP!
OW! JEEZ THAT HURTS.

1196
00:58:50,027 --> 00:58:52,130
WHAT'D YOU SAY?

1197
00:58:54,432 --> 00:58:56,935
[GOOFY LAUGHTER]

1198
00:58:58,235 --> 00:59:03,073
- HE'S GROWING GUITAR PICKS.
- [GROWLING]

1199
00:59:03,107 --> 00:59:05,208
ALL RIGHT!

1200
00:59:09,280 --> 00:59:11,648
OH, MY SCOLIOSIS. OW!

1201
00:59:17,788 --> 00:59:21,892
- [THUNDER BOOMING]
- OH, THERE'S A STORM
IN THE BATHROOM.

1202
00:59:21,927 --> 00:59:25,497
ARE YOU WEREWOLFING UP HERE?
BECAUSE YOUR DAMAGE DEPOSIT
DOES NOT COVER THAT.

1203
00:59:27,565 --> 00:59:30,702
I KNOW YOU'RE HOME.
WHERE ARE YOU?

1204
00:59:30,735 --> 00:59:32,637
IT'S ECONOMICAL NOT
TO HAVE A STORY LINE,

1205
00:59:32,670 --> 00:59:34,905
BECAUSE THEN YOU CAN JUST
FILM PEOPLE SAYING THINGS.

1206
00:59:37,242 --> 00:59:39,843
YEAH. SHE'S GOT A NECK
LIKE A MASAI WARRIOR.

1207
00:59:43,480 --> 00:59:45,917
WELL, I BETTER TAKE MY PANTS OFF
AND DO SOME TYPING.

1208
00:59:49,820 --> 00:59:52,757
I'M CRYING BECAUSE I MISS
HAVING NO PANTS ON.

1209
00:59:52,790 --> 00:59:56,193
- [CHUCKLING]
- [GROWLING]

1210
00:59:57,828 --> 01:00:00,030
- [GROWLING CONTINUES]
- [GASPS] OH, NO!

1211
01:00:00,063 --> 01:00:02,367
THE TOILET'S BACKING UP!

1212
01:00:04,735 --> 01:00:07,272
HEY, I'M JUST ON THE THRONE.
COME ON IN HERE AND TALK TO ME.

1213
01:00:15,145 --> 01:00:18,115
A MAURICE SENDAK CREATURE.

1214
01:00:18,115 --> 01:00:20,552
AW, MAN, YOU ONLY
RENT VICTIMS, LET ME TELL YA.

1215
01:00:22,653 --> 01:00:26,757
- [SNARLING]
- ZERO! I THINK YOU SHOULD PUT
TAYLOR BACK IN HIS CAGE.

1216
01:00:28,158 --> 01:00:31,662
- HEY! IT'S DON IMUS!
- NAH, NOT SCARY ENOUGH.

1217
01:00:37,768 --> 01:00:40,805
WOW, HERE WE GO.
THIS IS GOOD, BECAUSE IT'S BEEN
A COUPLE OF MINUTES

1218
01:00:40,838 --> 01:00:43,107
- SINCE A WOMAN WAS BRUTALIZED.
- YEAH.

1219
01:00:46,543 --> 01:00:49,047
SO, WEREWOLVES ARE
BASICALLY JACKSON BROWNE.

1220
01:00:51,182 --> 01:00:54,052
LIVE, FROM NEW YORK,
IT'S SATURDAY NIGHT.

1221
01:00:55,285 --> 01:00:58,288
I AM THE GREATEST!

1222
01:00:58,322 --> 01:01:00,492
YOU KNOW, YOU'D GET A LOT MORE
DONE IF YOU'D STOP REVELING

1223
01:01:00,525 --> 01:01:02,627
AFTER EACH SMALL VICTORY.

1224
01:01:05,563 --> 01:01:07,965
LUCKILY, HER BIG HAIR
CUSHIONED THE FALL.

1225
01:01:11,402 --> 01:01:14,072
OH, YEAH, I PUSHED HER DOWN
THE STAIRS. I'M THE MAN!

1226
01:01:16,473 --> 01:01:18,675
HE'S ALMOST AS HAIRY
AS ROBIN WILLIAMS.

1227
01:01:22,247 --> 01:01:24,382
- OKAY.
- ALL RIGHT.

1228
01:01:24,415 --> 01:01:27,318
- THANK YOU.
- AND NOW, BACK TO KUNG FU.

1229
01:01:27,352 --> 01:01:29,653
♪♪ [WHISTLING, AS AT
THE BEGINNING OF KUNG FU]

1230
01:01:29,687 --> 01:01:32,090
- DE NIRO. SNIPES. THE FAN.
- BUT THE MOON
IS A BEAUTIFUL SIGHT.

1231
01:01:32,123 --> 01:01:33,290
- COME ON!
- I'M HOME!

1232
01:01:33,323 --> 01:01:35,560
WHEN IT SINKS LOW
ON PLANET EARTH,

1233
01:01:35,593 --> 01:01:38,863
ALL HELL BREAKS LOOSE.

1234
01:01:38,897 --> 01:01:41,532
- STATISTICS SHOW THAT
MANY WILD THINGS HAPPEN...
- PAUL?

1235
01:01:41,565 --> 01:01:43,567
- WHEN THE MOON IS FULL...
- JACKET-WEARING LESSONS.

1236
01:01:45,035 --> 01:01:48,705
MANY SCIENTISTS BELIEVE
THAT MOON MADNESS IS A MYTH.

1237
01:01:51,042 --> 01:01:52,710
SOMEONE SO STRANGE
ON THE PHONE.

1238
01:01:52,743 --> 01:01:55,278
SHH! I'M WATCHING A GUY WATER
HIS LAWN. IT'S REALLY COOL.

1239
01:01:58,548 --> 01:02:01,885
...BEGINS THAT RITUAL WHERE
THE MOON'S EFFECT ON A HUMAN...

1240
01:02:01,918 --> 01:02:04,722
YOU LOOK LIKE HELL.
WHAT'S WRONG?

1241
01:02:04,722 --> 01:02:06,623
SHH!

1242
01:02:06,657 --> 01:02:08,325
PAUL!

1243
01:02:08,358 --> 01:02:10,862
SUBTLE SIGNS OF
BECOMING JUDD NELSON.

1244
01:02:10,895 --> 01:02:14,365
- [LAUGHING]
- I DON'T KNOW.

1245
01:02:14,398 --> 01:02:18,102
- IT'S LIKE A NIGHTMARE.
- AS IN SCHOOL, NUDE.

1246
01:02:18,135 --> 01:02:23,207
IT WAS A NIGHTMARE.
RUNNING IN THE STREETS,

1247
01:02:23,240 --> 01:02:26,377
- DOING THINGS--
- OH, NO! NOT THINGS!

1248
01:02:27,912 --> 01:02:30,313
CAN'T FIGURE IT OUT.

1249
01:02:31,815 --> 01:02:33,383
I REALLY AM SCARED.

1250
01:02:33,417 --> 01:02:36,487
DID I USE MY TONER
THIS MORNING?

1251
01:02:36,520 --> 01:02:38,722
MAYBE YOU WERE SLEEPWALKING.

1252
01:02:40,323 --> 01:02:43,260
- MY SOUFFLÉ!
- WHEN MY BROTHER
WAS ALIVE, AND HE WAS...

1253
01:02:43,293 --> 01:02:44,962
- WHAT TIME IS IT?
- [LAUGHING]

1254
01:02:44,995 --> 01:02:46,530
12:30. WHY?

1255
01:02:46,563 --> 01:02:48,833
THANKS FOR TURNING OFF
THE BAD SOUNDTRACK.

1256
01:02:51,535 --> 01:02:52,703
KNOW WHAT I REALLY
WANT TO DO?

1257
01:02:52,737 --> 01:02:54,605
...IS BABY, BE FRIENDS
WITH YOU.

1258
01:02:54,638 --> 01:02:57,542
I SEE THIS INDIAN
IN THE HOSPITAL.

1259
01:02:57,575 --> 01:02:58,877
I WANT TO KNOW
WHAT HAPPENED TO HIM.

1260
01:02:58,910 --> 01:03:01,012
ISAAC MIZRAHI
IN THE ROLE OF A LIFETIME!

1261
01:03:02,780 --> 01:03:05,415
WHAT DO YOU KNOW
ABOUT THIS, HUH?

1262
01:03:05,448 --> 01:03:07,117
COME ON, NATALIE,
WHAT DO YOU KNOW?

1263
01:03:07,152 --> 01:03:10,087
- WHAT ARE YOU HOLDING BACK?
- I'M NOT HOLDING BACK ANYTHING!

1264
01:03:10,120 --> 01:03:13,657
- CERTAINLY NOT TALENT.
- HE'S IN THE HOSPITAL
BECAUSE...

1265
01:03:13,690 --> 01:03:16,360
- BECAUSE WHAT?
- OKAY, I'LL TELL YOU.

1266
01:03:16,393 --> 01:03:18,228
BECAUSE IF I SAW FIVE,
YOU'LL SAY I'M FAT.

1267
01:03:18,262 --> 01:03:20,297
I TALK TO JOE AND BILLY
AS CO-WORKERS.

1268
01:03:20,330 --> 01:03:22,032
COME ON, COME ON,
SPIT IT OUT.

1269
01:03:22,065 --> 01:03:24,568
THEY SAID THEY SAW HIM
TURN INTO A BEAST!

1270
01:03:24,602 --> 01:03:26,103
TURN INTO BEETS?
THAT'S HORRIBLE!

1271
01:03:26,137 --> 01:03:28,672
WHEN HE ATTACKED THEM,
I HAD TO SHOOT HIM.

1272
01:03:28,705 --> 01:03:31,175
THAT'S WHY
HE'S IN THE HOSPITAL.

1273
01:03:33,777 --> 01:03:35,747
"FLAGSTAFF. INDUSTRY. FAMILY.

1274
01:03:35,780 --> 01:03:37,915
FOREIGN PEOPLE
TALKING IN ATTICS."

1275
01:03:37,948 --> 01:03:41,052
I'M SO SORRY I GOT YOU
INTO THIS MESS.

1276
01:03:41,085 --> 01:03:43,420
I'M VERY CONCERNED
ABOUT YOUR WELL-BEING.

1277
01:03:43,453 --> 01:03:46,090
- HIS WALLABEE?
- I'M GLAD TO HEAR THAT.

1278
01:03:46,123 --> 01:03:48,025
MY WALLABEE MEANS
A LOT TO ME.

1279
01:03:56,333 --> 01:03:59,037
[BIRDS SINGING]

1280
01:03:59,070 --> 01:04:01,838
[SERVO MAKING JUNGLE NOISES]

1281
01:04:03,840 --> 01:04:05,275
YEAH.

1282
01:04:05,308 --> 01:04:07,043
YEAH, LET'S GO
WITH ORANGE JHERI-CURL.

1283
01:04:07,077 --> 01:04:10,982
YEAH. WELL, LET ME TELL YOU
SOMETHING, AL.

1284
01:04:11,015 --> 01:04:13,083
WAIT. "HONEY, WHAT DO YOU THINK?
YELLOW MOHAWK?"

1285
01:04:13,117 --> 01:04:15,152
I THINK I'M GOING
TO TALK TO YOU LATER. YEAH.

1286
01:04:15,185 --> 01:04:17,288
YEAH, I'LL TALK TO YOU LATER.
BYE-BYE.

1287
01:04:19,157 --> 01:04:23,227
"YOUR DENTAL X-RAYS ARE BACK.
IT'S NOT GOOD."

1288
01:04:26,830 --> 01:04:28,933
URI, WHY ARE YOU
STARING AT ME LIKE THAT?

1289
01:04:28,967 --> 01:04:31,602
"IT'S AFTER LABOR DAY,
AND YOU'RE WEARING WHITE!"

1290
01:04:35,940 --> 01:04:39,477
I'M UH, GOING OUT
TO GET A LICENSE TO CARRY
A CONCEALED WEREWOLF SKULL.

1291
01:04:39,510 --> 01:04:41,478
SEE YOU.

1292
01:04:41,512 --> 01:04:44,915
[IMITATING WOMAN]
"I DON'T KNOW HOW TO LOVE HIM--"

1293
01:04:47,552 --> 01:04:49,620
[ALL]
PIRANHA!

1294
01:04:51,322 --> 01:04:53,757
UH, YOU'RE SITTING
IN MY PETRI DISH.

1295
01:04:55,727 --> 01:04:58,495
OH, HONEY, WHAT'S THE MATTER?
TALK TO NANA!

1296
01:05:02,400 --> 01:05:04,002
WHAT IS IT?
WHAT'S TROUBLING YOU?

1297
01:05:04,035 --> 01:05:05,402
OH, IT'S NOTHING.

1298
01:05:05,435 --> 01:05:07,338
NOW COME ON.
WHAT ARE YOU HOLDING BACK?

1299
01:05:07,372 --> 01:05:09,740
IT'S JUST THAT SO MANY THINGS
HAVE HAPPENED

1300
01:05:09,773 --> 01:05:11,508
SINCE WE DISCOVERED
THOSE REMAINS.

1301
01:05:11,542 --> 01:05:13,978
- NOT THINGS AGAIN!
- WOW.

1302
01:05:14,012 --> 01:05:18,148
TOM IS IN THE HOSPITAL, AND
PAUL'S BEEN ACTING VERY STRANGE.

1303
01:05:18,182 --> 01:05:19,850
THINKS HE'S TURNING
INTO A WEREWOLF, BEN.

1304
01:05:19,883 --> 01:05:21,418
[SWALLOWING SOUNDS]
"WEREWOLF!"

1305
01:05:21,452 --> 01:05:24,122
- YOU BELIEVE THAT?
- I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO BELIEVE ANYMORE.

1306
01:05:24,155 --> 01:05:26,957
TRY BELIEVING IN ESL
FOR A LITTLE WHILE.

1307
01:05:26,990 --> 01:05:30,160
DO YOU REALIZE
THAT IF THIS IS TRUE,

1308
01:05:30,193 --> 01:05:32,262
IT COULD BE THE GREATEST FIND
IN THE CENTURY.

1309
01:05:32,297 --> 01:05:34,798
BETTER THAN THE NEW,
BIGGER CHEEZ-ITS?

1310
01:05:34,832 --> 01:05:37,468
NOT TO MENTION THE MILLIONS OF
DOLLARS THAT WOULD BE AVAILABLE

1311
01:05:37,502 --> 01:05:39,437
JUST FOR RESEARCH.

1312
01:05:39,437 --> 01:05:41,572
I'M NOT CONCERNED WITH
MILLIONS OF DOLLARS!

1313
01:05:41,605 --> 01:05:43,673
I'M CONCERNED
WITH TOMMY AND PAUL!

1314
01:05:43,707 --> 01:05:45,910
AND CUBBY AND RONNIE
AND BIFF!

1315
01:05:45,943 --> 01:05:49,647
WHAT ARE YOU
HIDING FROM ME, NOEL?

1316
01:05:49,680 --> 01:05:53,483
- TELL ME THE TRUTH!
- "YOU CAN'T HANDLE THE TRUTH,
DEARIE."

1317
01:05:55,585 --> 01:05:57,888
IN DUE TIME,
YOU'LL KNOW EVERYTHING.

1318
01:05:57,922 --> 01:06:00,523
WELL, MAYBE THEN
IT'S TOO LATE!

1319
01:06:00,557 --> 01:06:03,893
WOW, THE FUTURE CONDITIONAL
PLUPERFECT SUBJUNCTIVE!

1320
01:06:06,730 --> 01:06:08,132
WELL.

1321
01:06:10,133 --> 01:06:12,637
SHTOPPEN BE TALKIN'
AND START WITH THE CHALKIN'.

1322
01:06:15,438 --> 01:06:17,240
YEE-HOO.

1323
01:06:17,273 --> 01:06:19,143
"THE COLOR OF HORNY."

1324
01:06:20,845 --> 01:06:23,180
YEAH, BIKERS LOVE
HARPSICHORD MUSIC.

1325
01:06:23,213 --> 01:06:25,683
HE PLAYS A WELL-TEMPERED
CLAVIER, MAN.

1326
01:06:32,590 --> 01:06:34,425
YOU'RE A HUSTLER.

1327
01:06:34,425 --> 01:06:36,393
THE CUE-- YOU'LL HAVE
TO PAY FOR THE CUE.

1328
01:06:39,097 --> 01:06:41,865
- IT WAS JUST A STROKE OF LUCK.
- UH-HUH.

1329
01:06:41,898 --> 01:06:45,068
- YOU'RE A HUSTLER.
- NO, I WAS IN HUSTLER.

1330
01:06:45,102 --> 01:06:48,738
- RACK 'EM OUT.
- THE UZEBEKISTANI
TRACY AND HEPBURN.

1331
01:06:52,510 --> 01:06:55,245
NEXT TO HIM,
I'M ALMOST SMART.

1332
01:07:02,387 --> 01:07:04,422
OH, THEY SUDDENLY TURNED
THE AIR CONDITIONING ON.

1333
01:07:07,725 --> 01:07:09,660
WILLIE MASCARPONE.

1334
01:07:13,563 --> 01:07:15,532
WAIT! NOW HE'S GOT GRAY HAIR!

1335
01:07:15,565 --> 01:07:18,402
ONE SIDE LEAVES.
THE WINNER STAYS.

1336
01:07:18,435 --> 01:07:21,705
OKAY, STOP. EVERYONE
GO UP A SHIRT SIZE.

1337
01:07:21,738 --> 01:07:25,208
- THAT'S THE AMERICAN WAY.
- ALTHOUGH WE HAVEN'T SEEN
AN AMERICAN IN THIS MOVIE YET.

1338
01:07:28,278 --> 01:07:30,580
IT'S ALL RIGHT, PAUL.
I CAN HANDLE THIS.

1339
01:07:32,683 --> 01:07:35,485
MM, RETSIN.

1340
01:07:35,518 --> 01:07:39,557
- YOU PLAY?
- GUESS OUR HERO WILL
GO BACK TO HIS WRITING NOW.

1341
01:07:39,590 --> 01:07:41,658
J.D. SALINGER WRITES MORE
THAN THIS GUY.

1342
01:07:43,527 --> 01:07:45,930
HEY, CHER HAS REALLY
LET HERSELF GO.

1343
01:07:47,898 --> 01:07:50,700
NOW THEY'RE PLAYING
THE SOUNDTRACK FROM KEN BURNS'
CIVIL WAR.

1344
01:07:53,103 --> 01:07:56,173
FAST EDDY FELSON'S SEX CHANGE
OPERATION WAS A BIG SUCCESS!

1345
01:08:02,112 --> 01:08:05,917
OH, WAIT, WAIT.
NO, NO. IS MY BEER
FRESHNESS-DATED?

1346
01:08:05,950 --> 01:08:08,352
OH, NO, I THINK
IT MIGHT BE SKUNKY!

1347
01:08:12,890 --> 01:08:16,593
- [PANTS]
- I MISS EUROPE!

1348
01:08:16,627 --> 01:08:20,230
♪ AROUND THE WORLD ♪

1349
01:08:20,263 --> 01:08:23,867
♪ I SEARCHED FOR YOU ♪

1350
01:08:25,035 --> 01:08:27,070
CHUBBY RAMONE.

1351
01:08:33,943 --> 01:08:36,347
WHO ADJUSTED THE FLAME SO HIGH
ON MY ZIPPO LIGHTER?

1352
01:08:38,548 --> 01:08:40,650
HE'S DREAMING OF
SLIMY CAT-PUPPETS!

1353
01:08:43,053 --> 01:08:45,522
SO, THEY'RE NOT NOTICING,
LIKE, HANDS RIPPING AWAY

1354
01:08:45,555 --> 01:08:47,492
RIGHT NEXT TO THEM?

1355
01:08:50,660 --> 01:08:52,730
HEY, PAUL, YOU'RE REALLY
TURNING INTO A WEREWOLF
OVER THERE--

1356
01:08:52,763 --> 01:08:54,832
ANYWAY, THREE-BALL
IN THE CORNER POCKET.

1357
01:08:56,767 --> 01:09:00,437
HEY, SHE WAS SOLID.
SHE WAS.

1358
01:09:00,470 --> 01:09:02,607
FREDERICK REMINGTON'S
GUERNICA.

1359
01:09:02,640 --> 01:09:04,308
NOT A GOOD SIGN WHEN
THE ACTION IN YOUR MOVIE

1360
01:09:04,342 --> 01:09:06,443
IS UPSTAGED BY A MURAL.

1361
01:09:10,280 --> 01:09:13,683
- IT'S THE ANGEL SITTING BULL.
- THANKS FOR KILLING ME
AND ALL MY PEOPLE!

1362
01:09:13,683 --> 01:09:17,522
ENJOY OUR LAND!

1363
01:09:17,555 --> 01:09:21,292
HEY, DID I HAVE TOO MUCH MESCAL?
OR DOES ANYONE ELSE SEE THOSE
INDIANS IN THE SKY OVER THERE?

1364
01:09:23,360 --> 01:09:25,295
- WYCLEF.
- HEY, BIKER.

1365
01:09:25,328 --> 01:09:27,330
HEY, RASTA.

1366
01:09:29,433 --> 01:09:32,002
YOU LOSE, YURI. AS ALWAYS.

1367
01:09:34,805 --> 01:09:37,575
- I'LL CATCH YOU NEXT TIME.
- ON PECTORAL THEATER!

1368
01:09:39,042 --> 01:09:41,145
THERE WILL BE
NO NEXT TIME, YURI.

1369
01:09:41,178 --> 01:09:44,648
- HI, GIRLFRIEND!
- HEY, YOU'RE GOOD.

1370
01:09:44,682 --> 01:09:48,285
LET'S SEE HOW GOOD
YOU REALLY ARE. I'LL RACK 'EM.

1371
01:09:48,318 --> 01:09:50,820
PEOPLE SAY "RACK"
TO ME A LOT. WHY?

1372
01:09:55,025 --> 01:09:57,862
AH, THE MOVIE
THAT TAKES ITS TIME
AND HANGS AROUND IN BARS.

1373
01:09:59,930 --> 01:10:04,802
AND THERE GOES ANOTHER ONE!
MAN, THE POOL CUE BUDGET
MUST BE ENORMOUS.

1374
01:10:04,835 --> 01:10:08,372
I'D LIKE THE FIVE BALL THERE,
AND THE 11 BALL HERE--

1375
01:10:08,438 --> 01:10:10,573
PERFECT!

1376
01:10:10,607 --> 01:10:15,312
- SO A WEREWOLF CO--
- OW, NO! HEY! WATCH IT! OW. OW.

1377
01:10:15,345 --> 01:10:16,647
GET A-- WATCH OUT.

1378
01:10:16,680 --> 01:10:19,383
MAN, YOU WERE RIGHT IN MY WAY.
I THINK I CUT MYSELF.

1379
01:10:29,893 --> 01:10:32,228
IT'S VERY SIMPLE, MIKE.
JUST DON'T FALL ON ME ANYMORE.

1380
01:10:32,262 --> 01:10:35,198
IF YOU WEREN'T SO SHARP
AND POINTY-- I THINK
I'LL NEED STITCHES.

1381
01:10:35,232 --> 01:10:39,337
WELL, PICK UP YOUR FEET
NEXT TIME, YOU BIG-- HEY!

1382
01:10:39,370 --> 01:10:41,272
HEY, MIKE,
THERE'S SOMETHING ABOUT YOU.

1383
01:10:41,305 --> 01:10:45,008
I DON'T KNOW, BUT SUDDENLY YOU
ARE A VERY, VERY HANDSOME MAN.

1384
01:10:45,042 --> 01:10:46,877
- REALLY?
- YEAH, I CAN'T BELIEVE
I NEVER NOTICED

1385
01:10:46,910 --> 01:10:50,147
HOW STRIKING YOU ARE!
I MEAN, YOU ARE A GOD!

1386
01:10:50,180 --> 01:10:54,117
- WELL, THANK YOU. I JUST--
- [SHRIEKS] MIKE,
LOOK AT YOUR HANDS!

1387
01:10:54,150 --> 01:10:57,487
- FEEL YOUR HEAD!
- HMM.

1388
01:10:57,520 --> 01:11:00,390
SO I HAVE CLAWS AND A NET!
WHAT'S THE BIG--
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE.

1389
01:11:00,390 --> 01:11:02,927
AH, WHEN YOU STUPIDLY
FELL ON ME, SOME OF MY ESSENCE

1390
01:11:02,927 --> 01:11:04,495
MUST HAVE MINGLED
WITH YOUR ESSENCE.

1391
01:11:04,528 --> 01:11:06,397
YUCK, DON'T SAY "ESSENCE."
BLECCH! PTAH!

1392
01:11:06,430 --> 01:11:10,867
WHY, YOU KNOW WHAT? I AM
BEGINNING TO LOOK AND FEEL
LIKE YOU-- AND YOU KNOW WHAT?

1393
01:11:10,900 --> 01:11:12,937
[MIKE AND CROW] I'M PERFECTLY
COMFORTABLE WITH THAT!

1394
01:11:12,970 --> 01:11:15,005
[IN UNISON]
YES, THAT'S EXACTLY
WHAT I THINK!

1395
01:11:15,038 --> 01:11:17,240
AAH! HE'S A WERECROW,
A WERECROW!

1396
01:11:17,273 --> 01:11:19,208
YES, OKAY?
TELL ME HOW YOUR FEEL.

1397
01:11:19,242 --> 01:11:21,178
- WELL, I FEEL THIN.
- UH-HUH.

1398
01:11:21,212 --> 01:11:23,047
- I HAVE
AN INTENSE LOVE FOR BACON.
- OH, YEAH.

1399
01:11:23,080 --> 01:11:25,515
AND A SENSE OF MORAL SUPERIORITY
OVER EVERYONE I MEET.

1400
01:11:25,548 --> 01:11:27,652
YES! PERFECT! YOU'RE ME!
[CHUCKLES]

1401
01:11:27,685 --> 01:11:30,187
- THIS IS TURNING OUT GREAT!
- OH, MAN, I LOVE US!

1402
01:11:30,220 --> 01:11:31,688
AND ME, CROW.
[KISS]

1403
01:11:31,722 --> 01:11:35,058
WILL YOU EXCUSE ME? I'M GOING
TO GO THROW UP ALL OVER MYSELF.

1404
01:11:35,092 --> 01:11:37,460
YEAH, WHATEVER.
SO WHAT ELSE CAN I EXPECT?

1405
01:11:37,493 --> 01:11:40,697
WELL, YOUR VOICE IS GOING
TO CHANGE INEXPLICABLY
EVERY SEVEN YEARS OR SO--

1406
01:11:40,730 --> 01:11:44,033
- OKAY, GOOD.
- YOU'LL START ORDERING SALAD
SPINNERS BY THE TRUCKLOAD...

1407
01:11:44,067 --> 01:11:45,468
- FROM QVC...
- ALREADY HAVE!

1408
01:11:45,502 --> 01:11:46,937
GREAT! UH-OH.

1409
01:11:46,970 --> 01:11:48,972
- OH, WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.
- WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

1410
01:11:49,005 --> 01:11:51,408
- WHAT ELSE?
- WELL, YOU'LL HAVE TO HIDE

1411
01:11:51,442 --> 01:11:53,243
YOUR HUGE COLLECTION
OF TATTOO MAGAZINES.

1412
01:11:53,277 --> 01:11:55,912
OH, GOOD POINT.
[LAUGHS]

1413
01:12:02,285 --> 01:12:04,955
[GAGGING]

1414
01:12:04,988 --> 01:12:07,825
OH, THIS IS EXACTLY
WHAT I WANTED TO SEE.

1415
01:12:07,858 --> 01:12:10,727
SO, ANY GIVEN BENNIGAN'S
BATHROOM ON ANY FRIDAY NIGHT.

1416
01:12:10,760 --> 01:12:11,962
- [RETCHING]
- SOUND FAMILIAR, MIKE?

1417
01:12:11,995 --> 01:12:14,465
- UH, CRO-- MI--
- [RETCHES]

1418
01:12:15,965 --> 01:12:18,235
OH, THANK YOU. THE SCENE
WASN'T REPULSIVE ENOUGH.

1419
01:12:18,268 --> 01:12:21,072
OH, IT'S JUST HIS
SECRET HAIR-DYEING PLACE.

1420
01:12:21,105 --> 01:12:23,907
[PANTING, LABORED BREATHING]

1421
01:12:27,343 --> 01:12:30,913
PAUL?
- YOU'RE BEAUTIFUL.

1422
01:12:30,947 --> 01:12:32,448
HEY, THANKS FOR STINKIN' UP
THE JOINT.

1423
01:12:32,482 --> 01:12:35,385
DO YOU KNOW HOW MUCH STRONGER
MY SENSE OF SMELL IS AS A WOLF?

1424
01:12:37,653 --> 01:12:40,990
WHY, IF I WASN'T A WEREWOLF,
I'D-- OH-- [MUMBLES]

1425
01:12:41,023 --> 01:12:43,560
OH, MY WERE-TUMMY.

1426
01:12:43,593 --> 01:12:47,297
TURNING INTO A WEREWOLF,
PLUS MY IRRITABLE BOWEL
SYNDROME'S ACTING UP TOO--

1427
01:12:50,633 --> 01:12:53,037
- [THUNDER]
- OH, BOY, HARPSICHORD
MUSIC TODAY.

1428
01:12:53,070 --> 01:12:55,838
[GROWLING]

1429
01:12:58,842 --> 01:13:00,843
- STILL A MESS. YEAH!
- [ROARING]

1430
01:13:02,212 --> 01:13:05,215
NEWSIES!

1431
01:13:05,248 --> 01:13:07,450
UH-HUH, YEAH, YEAH.
BUT HOW'S THE POOL GAME GOING?

1432
01:13:09,687 --> 01:13:12,857
- [WOLF HOWLING]
- GABBY HAYES, WEREWOLF.

1433
01:13:12,890 --> 01:13:15,758
NO, HE'S RUNNING THROUGH
THE STREETS DOING THINGS!

1434
01:13:18,128 --> 01:13:21,798
[LAUGHS]
AH, GREAT. A RANDOM CITIZEN
THAT CAN KICK A WEREWOLF'S ASS.

1435
01:13:29,707 --> 01:13:31,608
DIRECTED BY JACKIE CHAN.

1436
01:13:31,642 --> 01:13:33,043
HEY, MAN, WHAT THE HELL
ARE YOU DOING?

1437
01:13:33,077 --> 01:13:35,078
I AM PRAYING, ALL RIGHT?

1438
01:13:37,647 --> 01:13:39,082
BASQUIAT IS IN DANGER!

1439
01:13:40,683 --> 01:13:43,087
[WOLF HOWLS]

1440
01:13:43,087 --> 01:13:44,955
HE'S ATTACKING THE GRIP TRUCK!

1441
01:13:44,988 --> 01:13:48,325
"FROM LIGHTHOUSE GRIP AND
EQUIPMENT, SERVING THE FILM
INDUSTRY SINCE 1965."

1442
01:13:52,195 --> 01:13:54,965
I MADE IT, MA!
TOP OF THE FARMER'S BANK!

1443
01:13:57,100 --> 01:13:59,903
♪ WHERE THE STREETS
HAVE NO NAME ♪

1444
01:14:02,807 --> 01:14:07,177
NOEL, THIS IS NOT A FIGMENT
OF MY IMAGINATION!

1445
01:14:07,210 --> 01:14:10,813
BY WHAT HAPPENED TO TOMMY,
I SWEAR I SAW IT HAPPEN TO VIC,

1446
01:14:10,847 --> 01:14:14,050
THE SECURITY GUARD,
RIGHT BEFORE MY EYES.

1447
01:14:14,083 --> 01:14:17,387
THE POLICE HAVE
HIS BODY AT THE MORGUE.

1448
01:14:17,420 --> 01:14:20,823
PAUL HAS THE SAME SYMPTOMS--
MAYBE EVEN WORSE.

1449
01:14:20,857 --> 01:14:23,293
I KNOW WHERE PAUL IS,
AND I SUGGEST

1450
01:14:23,327 --> 01:14:26,163
YOU GET ALL THE UNITS READY
AND MEET ME AT PAUL'S

1451
01:14:26,197 --> 01:14:28,832
BEFORE WE LOSE HIM
LIKE WE LOST TOMMY AND VIC.

1452
01:14:28,865 --> 01:14:31,602
WE'LL SEE. IF PAUL
TURNS OUT TO BE A--

1453
01:14:31,635 --> 01:14:35,738
- AN ACTOR...
- NAALDLOOSHII, A WEREWOLF--

1454
01:14:35,772 --> 01:14:37,507
YOUR REWARD WILL BE
IMMEASURABLE.

1455
01:14:37,540 --> 01:14:41,945
PROFESSOR RIVERO,
I CAN'T WAIT TO SHOW YOU.

1456
01:14:41,978 --> 01:14:46,783
- OKAY, WHERE IS HE NOW?
- I'M SURE HE WENT BACK
TO HIS NEST TO HIDE.

1457
01:14:46,817 --> 01:14:49,820
NOW WE MUST GET TO HIM
BEFORE DAYBREAK.

1458
01:14:49,853 --> 01:14:51,622
BEFORE HE RETURNS TO NORMAL.

1459
01:14:51,655 --> 01:14:53,423
ALL RIGHT. I'M ON MY WAY.

1460
01:14:53,457 --> 01:14:55,225
I'M SORRY.
I HAD TO TAKE THAT CALL.

1461
01:14:55,258 --> 01:14:58,428
SO LET'S CONTINUE TO EXPLORE
YOUR FEELINGS ABOUT YOUR FATHER.

1462
01:14:58,462 --> 01:15:00,030
[HANGING UP]

1463
01:15:00,063 --> 01:15:02,832
HAVE YOU NOTICED THAT MY ACCENT
HAS GROWN AS BAD AS YOURS?

1464
01:15:02,867 --> 01:15:05,435
YURI, WHERE'S PAUL?

1465
01:15:05,468 --> 01:15:07,537
YOU'RE ASKIN' ME?

1466
01:15:07,570 --> 01:15:09,372
THIS IS NOT THE TIME
FOR GAMES.

1467
01:15:09,405 --> 01:15:10,873
WHAT GAMES?

1468
01:15:10,907 --> 01:15:12,142
WHAT HAPPENED TO HIM?

1469
01:15:12,175 --> 01:15:13,143
WHAT HIM?

1470
01:15:13,177 --> 01:15:14,143
IS HE IN DANGER?

1471
01:15:14,177 --> 01:15:15,478
WHAT DANGER?

1472
01:15:15,512 --> 01:15:17,313
THAT'S EXACTLY WHAT
I WANT TO TALK TO YOU ABOUT.

1473
01:15:17,347 --> 01:15:19,950
LOOK, HIS QUARTER'S UP
AND HE'S HOLDING UP THE TABLE.

1474
01:15:22,318 --> 01:15:23,887
LET'S TALK.

1475
01:15:23,920 --> 01:15:25,422
I WONDER WHAT LANGUAGE
THEY'LL USE.

1476
01:15:25,455 --> 01:15:29,125
AUSTRIAN. PORTUGUESE.
BULGARIAN. CATALAN.

1477
01:15:31,395 --> 01:15:35,565
MEANWHILE, SLASH IS STILL TRYING
IN VAIN TO SINK A BALL.

1478
01:15:39,335 --> 01:15:41,238
THEY HAVE THE GREATEST
PAD THAI HERE.

1479
01:15:41,272 --> 01:15:43,207
WE GOTTA TRY IT.

1480
01:15:45,308 --> 01:15:46,443
YOU WANT A DRINK?

1481
01:15:46,477 --> 01:15:48,578
NO. JUST SAY WHATEVER
YOU HAVE TO SAY.

1482
01:15:48,612 --> 01:15:50,680
WE DON'T HAVE A BIRTHDAY
OVER HERE, DO WE?

1483
01:15:50,713 --> 01:15:52,748
I'M SICK OF BIRTHDAYS.

1484
01:15:52,782 --> 01:15:54,652
WANT A DRINK?

1485
01:15:54,685 --> 01:15:55,718
NO. THANKS.

1486
01:15:55,752 --> 01:15:57,453
THAT'LL BE TWO NOTHINGS
AT TABLE SEVEN.

1487
01:15:57,487 --> 01:15:59,657
I KNOW THIS IS GOING
TO BE VERY DIFFICULT

1488
01:15:59,690 --> 01:16:00,857
FOR YOU TO UNDERSTAND...

1489
01:16:00,890 --> 01:16:01,925
BECAUSE OF MY ACCENT.

1490
01:16:01,958 --> 01:16:03,427
BUT FORGET ABOUT PAUL.

1491
01:16:03,460 --> 01:16:05,728
HE'S A FULL-BLOODED
WEREWOLF NOW.

1492
01:16:05,762 --> 01:16:07,597
YOU KNOW IT, I KNOW IT,
NOEL KNOWS IT.

1493
01:16:07,630 --> 01:16:09,298
AND IF YOU DON'T WANT WHAT
HAPPENED TO TOMMY

1494
01:16:09,332 --> 01:16:10,300
TO HAPPEN TO PAUL...

1495
01:16:10,333 --> 01:16:11,335
BUTTONS ARE NEAT.

1496
01:16:11,368 --> 01:16:13,137
HELP US GET HIM BACK
TO THE LAB.

1497
01:16:13,170 --> 01:16:16,540
PUT HIM IN A CAGE,
HOLD A PRESS CONFERENCE,

1498
01:16:16,573 --> 01:16:19,910
AND LET THE WORLD SEE
WHAT WE'VE ACHIEVED.

1499
01:16:19,943 --> 01:16:20,910
NOW, HOLD ON.

1500
01:16:20,943 --> 01:16:21,912
THERE'S MORE.

1501
01:16:21,945 --> 01:16:22,947
NOEL AND SOME OF THE GUARDS

1502
01:16:22,980 --> 01:16:24,748
ARE ON THEIR WAY TO GRAB PAUL

1503
01:16:24,782 --> 01:16:27,417
AND TAKE HIM TO THE LAB.

1504
01:16:27,450 --> 01:16:30,453
I RESENT VIOLENCE. I DON'T WANT
ANYTHING TO HAPPEN TO HIM.

1505
01:16:30,487 --> 01:16:32,588
HE'S ALL WE'VE GOT.

1506
01:16:32,622 --> 01:16:35,892
AND I'M SURE YOU DON'T WANT
ANYTHING TO HAPPEN TO HIM,
EITHER.

1507
01:16:35,925 --> 01:16:37,393
SO IT ALL COMES TO THIS?

1508
01:16:37,427 --> 01:16:39,663
THE THING THAT IT COMES TO?

1509
01:16:39,697 --> 01:16:43,033
YOU AND NOEL IS IN IT FOR FAME
AND FORTUNE?

1510
01:16:43,067 --> 01:16:45,168
YES. WE IS.

1511
01:16:45,202 --> 01:16:46,168
BUT OVER MY DEAD BODY.

1512
01:16:46,202 --> 01:16:48,038
[LAUGHS]

1513
01:16:48,072 --> 01:16:50,873
YOU HEAR ME?
I WON'T STAND FOR IT.

1514
01:16:50,907 --> 01:16:52,475
YOU IS A JERK.

1515
01:16:52,508 --> 01:16:55,478
HEY, NATALIE. HEY, NATALIE.

1516
01:16:55,512 --> 01:16:58,448
I IS GOING TO FIND PAUL.

1517
01:16:58,482 --> 01:17:00,317
PAUL!

1518
01:17:00,350 --> 01:17:04,053
THERE'S A BUSINESS UP THERE
SIMPLY CALLED "R."

1519
01:17:07,657 --> 01:17:11,060
OH, LOVELY.
IT'S TWO-FOR-ONE BRAIN HAMMERS
TONIGHT, MARTHA.

1520
01:17:12,295 --> 01:17:13,397
OH, HE'S DUSTING.

1521
01:17:13,430 --> 01:17:15,098
YEAH, HIS PERSONAL HYGIENE
IS HORRIBLE,

1522
01:17:15,132 --> 01:17:17,333
BUT HE'S OTHERWISE
A NEAT FREAK.

1523
01:17:17,400 --> 01:17:19,002
[GROWLING]

1524
01:17:19,035 --> 01:17:21,738
AH, JUST MADE
THE CALL TO PRAYER. WHEW.

1525
01:17:21,772 --> 01:17:25,075
WHAT'S GOIN' ON?

1526
01:17:25,108 --> 01:17:27,210
OH, MY GOD.

1527
01:17:27,243 --> 01:17:30,080
THIS IS SO GREAT.

1528
01:17:30,113 --> 01:17:33,750
HOLY [...] GOD FATHER.

1529
01:17:35,418 --> 01:17:36,987
WEREWOLF?

1530
01:17:37,020 --> 01:17:38,488
NO, I'M A SQUIRREL MONKEY.

1531
01:17:38,522 --> 01:17:40,523
OF COURSE I'M A WEREWOLF.

1532
01:17:43,293 --> 01:17:44,895
LELAND SKLAR--SURVIVALIST.

1533
01:17:44,928 --> 01:17:46,830
OH, NO. SAVE ME.

1534
01:17:46,863 --> 01:17:49,933
UH, THIS IS GOD. I'VE REVIEWED
IT WITH THE COMMITTEE, AND NO.

1535
01:17:49,967 --> 01:17:50,933
WE WON'T SAVE YOU.

1536
01:17:50,967 --> 01:17:52,935
IF THIS THING IS A WEREWOLF...

1537
01:17:52,968 --> 01:17:54,303
AAH!

1538
01:17:54,337 --> 01:17:56,873
UH, WOULD YOU MIND EATING THIS
JAR OF MEAT-TENDERIZER

1539
01:17:56,907 --> 01:17:58,442
BEFORE I KILL YOU?

1540
01:17:58,475 --> 01:17:59,710
[GROWLING]

1541
01:17:59,743 --> 01:18:01,343
WHOEVER YOU ARE,
UGH,

1542
01:18:01,378 --> 01:18:02,678
DON'T HURT ME.

1543
01:18:02,712 --> 01:18:03,947
PLEASE!

1544
01:18:03,980 --> 01:18:06,817
DON'T.
DON'T, DON'T, DON'T.

1545
01:18:06,850 --> 01:18:08,385
PLEASE.

1546
01:18:08,418 --> 01:18:10,387
HE'S GOT MOVEMENTS
LIKE ANTHONY KIEDIS.

1547
01:18:10,453 --> 01:18:12,388
♪ DOO DOO DOO DOO
DOO DOO DOO ♪

1548
01:18:12,422 --> 01:18:13,657
THE DEATH OF OLIVER SACKS.

1549
01:18:13,690 --> 01:18:15,558
DON'T HURT ME. PLEASE.

1550
01:18:15,592 --> 01:18:17,560
MR. NILES.
IS THAT YOU?

1551
01:18:17,593 --> 01:18:18,995
WAIT, NOT FAIR.
HE'S STILL ALIVE.

1552
01:18:19,028 --> 01:18:19,997
YEAH.

1553
01:18:20,030 --> 01:18:22,298
I'M SAM. THE KEEPER.

1554
01:18:22,332 --> 01:18:25,302
HIS POWERFUL BODILY FUNK
FINALLY COMES IN HANDY.

1555
01:18:25,335 --> 01:18:26,470
I'M THE GOOD GUY.

1556
01:18:26,503 --> 01:18:27,437
RIGHT, FOLKS?

1557
01:18:35,778 --> 01:18:38,315
OH, MAN. RUNNING THROUGH
THE STREETS DOING THINGS

1558
01:18:38,348 --> 01:18:40,283
REALLY TAKES IT OUT OF YA.

1559
01:18:45,588 --> 01:18:48,325
BOY. I'D HATE TO SEE
HIS SINK TRAP.

1560
01:18:48,358 --> 01:18:50,560
[LAUGHS]

1561
01:18:50,593 --> 01:18:53,763
OH, WHY DID I EVER EAT THAT
EXTRA GAZELLE?

1562
01:18:53,797 --> 01:18:55,132
[GROWLING]

1563
01:18:55,165 --> 01:18:59,803
I'VE BEEN A BAD BOY.
I'M GIVING MYSELF A TIMEOUT.

1564
01:18:59,837 --> 01:19:03,707
FELLOW FREEMAN BROTHER
MILITIA MEN, COME TO MY AID.

1565
01:19:07,610 --> 01:19:09,612
HONEY,
I IS BEING HOME.

1566
01:19:11,882 --> 01:19:14,818
SHE HAS TO REST UP FOR HER MATCH
WITH MINNESOTA FATS TOMORROW

1567
01:19:17,520 --> 01:19:19,122
OH, GOD OF BATTLES.

1568
01:19:19,155 --> 01:19:21,223
OH. MISS NATALIE.

1569
01:19:21,257 --> 01:19:22,792
I DON'T THINK YOU SHOULD
GO UP THERE.

1570
01:19:22,825 --> 01:19:24,962
SOMETHING HORRIBLE
HAS HAPPENED.

1571
01:19:24,995 --> 01:19:25,995
I PASSED MY TAPEWORM.

1572
01:19:26,028 --> 01:19:27,597
I WAS JUST PRAYIN'
FOR THE POLICE.

1573
01:19:27,630 --> 01:19:30,200
I THINK WE SHOULD
CALL THE COPS.

1574
01:19:30,233 --> 01:19:32,868
NO, SAM.
DON'T CALL THE POLICE.

1575
01:19:32,902 --> 01:19:34,003
I'LL TAKE CARE OF HIM.

1576
01:19:34,037 --> 01:19:35,038
DON'T WORRY ABOUT IT.

1577
01:19:35,072 --> 01:19:36,238
IS THE GUN LOADED?

1578
01:19:36,272 --> 01:19:37,773
THIS?
SURE, IT'S LOADED.

1579
01:19:37,807 --> 01:19:39,810
I WANT YOU
TO GO TO THE WINDOW,

1580
01:19:39,843 --> 01:19:41,243
AND IF ANYBODY
TRIES TO BREAK IN,

1581
01:19:41,277 --> 01:19:42,245
SHOOT 'EM.

1582
01:19:42,278 --> 01:19:43,913
YOU GOT IT,
MISS NATALIE.

1583
01:19:43,947 --> 01:19:46,883
'CAUSE THE REAL DANGER IS FROM
THE NON-WEREWOLVES OUTSIDE.

1584
01:19:46,917 --> 01:19:47,917
RIGHT.

1585
01:19:47,950 --> 01:19:49,887
[GROWLING]

1586
01:19:52,455 --> 01:19:53,557
PAUL?

1587
01:19:53,590 --> 01:19:56,493
FREDDY KRUEGER.
HELLRAISER.

1588
01:19:56,560 --> 01:19:57,660
PAUL.

1589
01:19:57,660 --> 01:19:58,628
[LAUGHS]

1590
01:19:58,695 --> 01:20:00,630
PAUL?
IS YOU AT THIS PLACE?

1591
01:20:03,667 --> 01:20:06,603
OH, THAT FIEND RICK BAKER
TACKLED HIM AND DID THIS TO HIM.

1592
01:20:08,003 --> 01:20:09,472
[GROWLING]

1593
01:20:09,505 --> 01:20:11,808
STARRING RESUSCI ANNIE.

1594
01:20:11,842 --> 01:20:14,143
OH, MY GOD.

1595
01:20:14,177 --> 01:20:16,647
DON'T LOOK.
I HAVEN'T BEEN GROOMED.

1596
01:20:18,482 --> 01:20:19,850
STILL SHE'S MORE EMOTIVE THAN
GILLIAN ANDERSON.

1597
01:20:19,883 --> 01:20:20,850
YUP.

1598
01:20:20,883 --> 01:20:21,818
UH-HUH.

1599
01:20:23,353 --> 01:20:26,022
PAUL.
YOU IS A "WEREWILF."

1600
01:20:26,055 --> 01:20:28,492
[LAUGHS]

1601
01:20:28,525 --> 01:20:31,460
SAY, THAT PHONE UP THERE
IS STACKED.

1602
01:20:31,493 --> 01:20:33,330
HEY, MIKE, WOULD YOU
INTRODUCE ME TO THAT PHONE?

1603
01:20:33,363 --> 01:20:34,330
CUT THAT OUT.

1604
01:20:34,363 --> 01:20:35,298
HI THERE.

1605
01:20:35,332 --> 01:20:36,265
PAUL.

1606
01:20:39,002 --> 01:20:41,638
IS THAT A 1x6?
OH, IT'S HER ACTING.

1607
01:20:41,672 --> 01:20:43,240
YEAH.

1608
01:20:43,273 --> 01:20:45,742
PAUL.
PLEASE DON'T HURT ME.

1609
01:20:45,775 --> 01:20:48,110
THINK OF MY FAMILY
IN LATVIA.

1610
01:20:48,143 --> 01:20:51,213
I LOVE YOU
NO MATTER WHAT.

1611
01:20:51,213 --> 01:20:53,517
WELL, CAN YOU HELP ME GET
THESE BUGLES OFF MY FINGERS?

1612
01:20:53,550 --> 01:20:55,685
[LAUGHS]

1613
01:20:55,718 --> 01:20:57,087
ITCHY, THESE ANTS.

1614
01:20:57,120 --> 01:21:00,890
YURI AND NOEL WANT TO TAKE YOU
TO THE LAB AND CAGE YOU.

1615
01:21:00,923 --> 01:21:03,125
SHE LEARNED ENGLISH FROM
THE WILD AND CRAZY GUYS.

1616
01:21:03,158 --> 01:21:04,827
[SOBS]

1617
01:21:04,860 --> 01:21:07,263
WOULD YOU PUT ON A LONG,
LOOSE-FITTING GOWN

1618
01:21:07,297 --> 01:21:09,832
AND ROLL AROUND
IN THE MUD FOR ME?

1619
01:21:09,865 --> 01:21:12,268
I AM HERE TO HELP.

1620
01:21:12,302 --> 01:21:14,670
I DON'T KNOW HOW,

1621
01:21:14,703 --> 01:21:17,307
BUT I KNOW I GOTTA GET YOU
OUT OF HERE.

1622
01:21:17,340 --> 01:21:18,575
THIS IS VERY MOVING.

1623
01:21:18,608 --> 01:21:19,742
MEANING THAT I WANT TO MOVE

1624
01:21:19,775 --> 01:21:20,743
OUT OF THE THEATER
IMMEDIATELY.

1625
01:21:20,777 --> 01:21:21,745
YES.

1626
01:21:21,778 --> 01:21:23,713
THEY'RE GONNA
BE HERE SOON.

1627
01:21:25,415 --> 01:21:26,348
RANDY?

1628
01:21:27,650 --> 01:21:30,853
CINEMATOGRAPHY BY
HASKELL WEXLER'S CAT.

1629
01:21:32,255 --> 01:21:35,258
AND JIMMY CARTER COMES IN
TO NEGOTIATE AN AGREEMENT.

1630
01:21:39,428 --> 01:21:41,530
I CAN'T BELIEVE
PEOPLE CALL ME A PSYCHO.

1631
01:21:41,563 --> 01:21:42,732
I'M GONNA TAKE
THOSE PEOPLE'S HEADS

1632
01:21:42,765 --> 01:21:44,367
AND CARVE 'EM INTO ASHTRAYS.

1633
01:21:46,102 --> 01:21:48,237
SHE'S SUDDENLY
IN PHILIP MARLOWE'S OFFICE?

1634
01:21:48,272 --> 01:21:50,340
SORT OF BIMBO NOIR, HERE.

1635
01:21:57,613 --> 01:22:00,750
UH, SWINGIN' BY TO SEE FLOUNDER
AND BLUTO AND PINTO.

1636
01:22:06,122 --> 01:22:07,523
OH, POOR GIRL.

1637
01:22:07,557 --> 01:22:09,225
LAST GUY SHE DATED
TURNED OUT TO BE

1638
01:22:09,258 --> 01:22:10,860
THE LOCH NESS MONSTER.

1639
01:22:12,562 --> 01:22:14,230
SORRY I CHEWED YOUR SHOE.
I'M SORRY.

1640
01:22:17,233 --> 01:22:19,568
MM. SAM GOT HIMSELF
SOME SEAMLESS GUTTERS.

1641
01:22:19,602 --> 01:22:21,537
NICE.

1642
01:22:24,107 --> 01:22:26,608
NEVER THROW HIS FETCH BALL
AGAINST THE PICTURE WINDOW.

1643
01:22:29,845 --> 01:22:31,013
HUH.

1644
01:22:31,047 --> 01:22:32,882
[LAUGHS]

1645
01:22:32,915 --> 01:22:33,917
UM, EXCUSE ME,

1646
01:22:33,950 --> 01:22:35,118
DID ANYONE SEE
A GLASS SHARD-ENCRUSTED

1647
01:22:35,152 --> 01:22:37,353
YETIGLANCHI GO BY?

1648
01:22:43,460 --> 01:22:47,663
OH, HIS APARTMENT IS RIGHT
NEXT TO MONUMENT VALLEY.

1649
01:22:47,697 --> 01:22:50,733
HIS JACKET MAKES HIM LOOK
LIKE A "WERE-WAITER."

1650
01:22:57,907 --> 01:22:59,242
WELL, FOLKS.
SHOULD I FOLLOW HIM?

1651
01:22:59,275 --> 01:23:00,610
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1652
01:23:06,348 --> 01:23:08,217
IT'S FRUIT BRUTE!

1653
01:23:08,250 --> 01:23:09,885
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]

1654
01:23:12,755 --> 01:23:15,025
CRICKETS ARE TRYING
TO DROWN OUT THE SOUNDTRACK.

1655
01:23:15,058 --> 01:23:16,993
GO CRICKETS.

1656
01:23:20,197 --> 01:23:22,665
THIS IS WHERE YURI'S
RUSSO-MEXICAN TRACKING SKILLS

1657
01:23:22,698 --> 01:23:24,700
WILL COME IN HANDY.

1658
01:23:28,037 --> 01:23:29,238
HMM?

1659
01:23:32,708 --> 01:23:35,512
FULLY A BEAR NOW.

1660
01:23:35,545 --> 01:23:37,613
DISGUISE MYSELF
WITH MY OWN ARMS.

1661
01:23:39,382 --> 01:23:41,852
AND A BAT, AGAIN.

1662
01:23:41,885 --> 01:23:44,553
♪ WONDER WOMAN ♪

1663
01:23:45,822 --> 01:23:47,290
OH, THERE'S A GRAFFITI-FILLED
UNDERPASS

1664
01:23:47,323 --> 01:23:49,125
IN THE DEEP WOODS.

1665
01:23:49,158 --> 01:23:50,460
[GROWLING]

1666
01:23:50,493 --> 01:23:52,328
HANG ON.
MY CONTACTS FELL OUT.

1667
01:23:52,362 --> 01:23:53,295
HANG ON.

1668
01:23:59,035 --> 01:24:01,805
HE'S JUST SCRATCHING HIMSELF
WITH HIS OWN WRISTWATCH.

1669
01:24:01,838 --> 01:24:02,872
[LAUGHS]

1670
01:24:02,905 --> 01:24:04,673
UGH.

1671
01:24:04,707 --> 01:24:07,243
END OF THE EURO-CHUCK WEPNER.

1672
01:24:08,745 --> 01:24:10,113
[GROWLING]

1673
01:24:10,147 --> 01:24:11,513
UGH.

1674
01:24:11,547 --> 01:24:14,817
TRYING TO GET IN ONE LAST
HAIR COLORING BEFORE HE DIES.

1675
01:24:17,553 --> 01:24:20,890
BLOOD CAME OUT
OF A RALPH STEADMAN DRAWING.

1676
01:24:25,862 --> 01:24:27,830
COMANCHE.

1677
01:24:27,863 --> 01:24:29,798
[GASPS]

1678
01:24:30,933 --> 01:24:32,868
WELL, HE GOT BETWEEN
PAUL AND HIS CUB.

1679
01:24:34,737 --> 01:24:37,173
EVEN IN DEATH
HE'S SUCKING HIS GUT IN.

1680
01:24:37,207 --> 01:24:38,373
[LAUGHS]

1681
01:24:39,442 --> 01:24:41,310
FORTUNATELY
THE DIRECTOR WANTED

1682
01:24:41,343 --> 01:24:43,245
NO REACTION IN THIS SCENE.

1683
01:24:43,278 --> 01:24:44,280
REMEMBER, CINDY.
NOTHING GETS IN.

1684
01:24:44,313 --> 01:24:46,715
NO INFORMATION
EVER REACHES YOUR BRAIN.

1685
01:24:46,748 --> 01:24:48,017
GOOD.

1686
01:24:49,352 --> 01:24:51,988
AND CONGRESS ENACTED
THE POP ROCKS LABELING LAW.

1687
01:24:52,022 --> 01:24:53,022
[LAUGHS]

1688
01:24:53,055 --> 01:24:54,990
[FOOTSTEPS]

1689
01:25:01,063 --> 01:25:03,700
I HAVE A FEELING THAT EVERY BIT
OF HER INTELLIGENCE

1690
01:25:03,733 --> 01:25:05,702
IS BEING USED TO CLIMB
THESE STAIRS.

1691
01:25:05,735 --> 01:25:07,670
MM-HMM.

1692
01:25:13,510 --> 01:25:14,643
SHOULD I?
YES.

1693
01:25:14,677 --> 01:25:16,612
I'LL TAKE THE NEXT STEP.

1694
01:25:19,048 --> 01:25:21,885
SHOE CAM.
ACTUAL SHOES.

1695
01:25:21,918 --> 01:25:24,087
LOOKS LIKE SHE WEARS
A SIZE 38

1696
01:25:24,120 --> 01:25:26,188
OR WHATEVER THE HELL SIZES
THEY USE OVER THERE.

1697
01:25:26,222 --> 01:25:28,157
CH-YEAH.

1698
01:25:30,293 --> 01:25:31,427
OKAY. SHE'S A WEREWOLF.

1699
01:25:31,460 --> 01:25:33,497
I THINK WE'RE ALL AHEAD OF YA,
MOVIE.

1700
01:25:33,530 --> 01:25:35,498
SORRY.

1701
01:25:35,532 --> 01:25:37,700
SHE HAS DILBERT-BOSS HORNS.

1702
01:25:39,568 --> 01:25:41,803
MINI BLINDS ARE FUN TO WATCH.

1703
01:25:44,373 --> 01:25:46,475
LOOK. HE HAS A LITTLE BOTTLE
OF MRS. BUTTERWORTH'S

1704
01:25:46,508 --> 01:25:48,043
ON HIS NIGHT TABLE.

1705
01:25:48,077 --> 01:25:50,913
[THUMP]

1706
01:25:50,947 --> 01:25:52,348
UH, THAT WAS THE SOUND
OF THE DIRECTOR

1707
01:25:52,382 --> 01:25:53,348
GIVING UP AND LEAVING.

1708
01:25:53,382 --> 01:25:54,717
[LAUGHS]

1709
01:25:54,750 --> 01:25:57,887
DID THIS MOVIE NOT PAY
ITS ELECTRICAL BILL?

1710
01:25:57,920 --> 01:26:00,190
PAUL.

1711
01:26:00,223 --> 01:26:01,457
OKAY MOVIE,
SHE'S A WEREWOLF.

1712
01:26:01,490 --> 01:26:03,527
WE REALLY GOTTA CALL TIME
ON THIS ONE.

1713
01:26:03,560 --> 01:26:04,893
I'M SORRY.

1714
01:26:04,927 --> 01:26:08,898
WELL, NOW, NOW, MAYBE SHE TURNED
INTO EDDIE VAN HALEN, SEE?

1715
01:26:08,932 --> 01:26:10,267
YEAH,
AND SHE TEASED HER HAIR,

1716
01:26:10,300 --> 01:26:14,037
THEN GOT DOWNRIGHT SADISTIC
WITH IT.

1717
01:26:14,070 --> 01:26:15,272
OH, COME ON.

1718
01:26:15,305 --> 01:26:19,008
DEAD PEOPLE KNOW
WHAT'S GOING TO HAPPEN HERE.

1719
01:26:19,042 --> 01:26:21,643
HEY, IF SHE'S A WOLF SHE'LL HAVE
THREE ROWS OF BREASTS.

1720
01:26:21,677 --> 01:26:22,645
[LAUGHS]

1721
01:26:22,678 --> 01:26:23,713
EW.

1722
01:26:23,747 --> 01:26:25,047
I'M NOT SURE
HOW TO FEEL ABOUT THAT.

1723
01:26:25,080 --> 01:26:26,582
YEAH, IT'S KINDA...

1724
01:26:26,615 --> 01:26:28,985
SHE'S MEETING
MAYNARD G. KREBS.

1725
01:26:29,018 --> 01:26:31,353
HMM.

1726
01:26:31,387 --> 01:26:34,090
HE'S BECOME
A "WERE-AMISH" GUY.

1727
01:26:37,360 --> 01:26:39,095
IT'S GONNA BE A LITTLE
SPIRIT GUMMY

1728
01:26:39,128 --> 01:26:41,063
WHEN I FIRST KISS YA.

1729
01:26:42,498 --> 01:26:43,633
[SIGHS]

1730
01:26:43,667 --> 01:26:45,435
SURPRISE ENDING
WRITTEN AND CONCEIVED

1731
01:26:45,468 --> 01:26:47,437
BY A TUBEWORM.

1732
01:26:47,470 --> 01:26:49,272
UGH!
I STAND CORRECTED.

1733
01:26:49,305 --> 01:26:53,475
SHE'S NOT A WEREWOLF.
SHE MERELY JOINED
THE CAST OF CATS.

1734
01:26:53,508 --> 01:26:56,845
MR. AND MRS. B.O. PLENTY.

1735
01:26:59,948 --> 01:27:02,652
♪ POW WOW THE INDIAN BOY ♪

1736
01:27:02,685 --> 01:27:05,722
♪ LOVED ALL THE ANIMALS
IN THE WEST ♪

1737
01:27:05,755 --> 01:27:08,792
♪ WE WILL WE WILL ♪

1738
01:27:08,825 --> 01:27:10,527
♪ ROCK YOU ♪

1739
01:27:10,560 --> 01:27:11,627
♪ TUSK ♪

1740
01:27:11,660 --> 01:27:13,128
♪ WELL THEY RAN THROUGH
THE BRIARS ♪

1741
01:27:13,162 --> 01:27:14,497
♪ AND THEY RAN
THROUGH THE BRAMBLES ♪

1742
